---The `Charge` object represents a single attempt to move money into your Stripe account.
---PaymentIntent confirmation is the most common way to create Charges, but [Account Debits](https://docs.stripe.com/connect/account-debits) may also create Charges.
---The create and capture methods are deprecated and will be deleted soon. If your integration uses either of them, you need to update it to use a different payment flow, such as [the Payment Intents API](https://docs.stripe.com/payments/payment-intents).
---@class stripe.Charge
---@field amount number Amount intended to be collected by this payment. A positive integer representing how much to charge in the [smallest currency unit](https://docs.stripe.com/currencies#zero-decimal) (e.g., 100 cents to charge $1.00 or 100 to charge ¥100, a zero-decimal currency). The minimum amount is $0.50 US or [equivalent in charge currency](https://docs.stripe.com/currencies#minimum-and-maximum-charge-amounts). The amount value supports up to eight digits (e.g., a value of 99999999 for a USD charge of $999,999.99).
---@field amount_captured number Amount in cents (or local equivalent) captured (can be less than the amount attribute on the charge if a partial capture was made).
---@field amount_refunded number Amount in cents (or local equivalent) refunded (can be less than the amount attribute on the charge if a partial refund was issued).
---@field application stripe.ChargeApplication|distilled.Null ID of the Connect application that created the charge.
---@field application_fee stripe.ChargeApplicationFee|distilled.Null The application fee (if any) for the charge. [See the Connect documentation](https://docs.stripe.com/connect/direct-charges#collect-fees) for details.
---@field application_fee_amount number|distilled.Null The amount of the application fee (if any) requested for the charge. [See the Connect documentation](https://docs.stripe.com/connect/direct-charges#collect-fees) for details.
---@field authorization_code? string Authorization code on the charge.
---@field balance_transaction stripe.ChargeBalanceTransaction|distilled.Null ID of the balance transaction that describes the impact of this charge on your account balance (not including refunds or disputes).
---@field billing_details stripe.BillingDetails
---@field calculated_statement_descriptor string|distilled.Null The full statement descriptor that is passed to card networks, and that is displayed on your customers' credit card and bank statements. Allows you to see what the statement descriptor looks like after the static and dynamic portions are combined. This value only exists for card payments.
---@field captured boolean If the charge was created without capturing, this Boolean represents whether it is still uncaptured or has since been captured.
---@field created number Time at which the object was created. Measured in seconds since the Unix epoch.
---@field currency string Three-letter [ISO currency code](https://www.iso.org/iso-4217-currency-codes.html), in lowercase. Must be a [supported currency](https://stripe.com/docs/currencies).
---@field customer stripe.ChargeCustomer|distilled.Null ID of the customer this charge is for if one exists.
---@field description string|distilled.Null An arbitrary string attached to the object. Often useful for displaying to users.
---@field disputed boolean Whether the charge has been disputed.
---@field failure_balance_transaction stripe.ChargeFailureBalanceTransaction|distilled.Null ID of the balance transaction that describes the reversal of the balance on your account due to payment failure.
---@field failure_code string|distilled.Null Error code explaining reason for charge failure if available (see [the errors section](https://docs.stripe.com/error-codes) for a list of codes).
---@field failure_message string|distilled.Null Message to user further explaining reason for charge failure if available.
---@field fraud_details stripe.ChargeFraudDetails|distilled.Null Information on fraud assessments for the charge.
---@field id string Unique identifier for the object.
---@field level3? stripe.Level3
---@field livemode boolean If the object exists in live mode, the value is `true`. If the object exists in test mode, the value is `false`.
---@field metadata stripe.ChargeMetadataMap Set of [key-value pairs](https://docs.stripe.com/api/metadata) that you can attach to an object. This can be useful for storing additional information about the object in a structured format.
---@field object stripe.ChargeObject String representing the object's type. Objects of the same type share the same value.
---@field on_behalf_of stripe.ChargeOnBehalfOf|distilled.Null The account (if any) the charge was made on behalf of without triggering an automatic transfer. See the [Connect documentation](https://docs.stripe.com/connect/separate-charges-and-transfers) for details.
---@field outcome stripe.ChargeOutcome|distilled.Null Details about whether the payment was accepted, and why. See [understanding declines](https://docs.stripe.com/declines) for details.
---@field paid boolean `true` if the charge succeeded, or was successfully authorized for later capture.
---@field payment_intent stripe.ChargePaymentIntent|distilled.Null ID of the PaymentIntent associated with this charge, if one exists.
---@field payment_method string|distilled.Null ID of the payment method used in this charge.
---@field payment_method_details stripe.PaymentMethodDetails|distilled.Null Details about the payment method at the time of the transaction.
---@field presentment_details? stripe.PaymentFlowsPaymentIntentPresentmentDetails
---@field radar_options? stripe.RadarRadarOptions
---@field receipt_email string|distilled.Null This is the email address that the receipt for this charge was sent to.
---@field receipt_number string|distilled.Null This is the transaction number that appears on email receipts sent for this charge. This attribute will be `null` until a receipt has been sent.
---@field receipt_url string|distilled.Null This is the URL to view the receipt for this charge. The receipt is kept up-to-date to the latest state of the charge, including any refunds. If the charge is for an Invoice, the receipt will be stylized as an Invoice receipt.
---@field refunded boolean Whether the charge has been fully refunded. If the charge is only partially refunded, this attribute will still be false.
---@field refunds? stripe.ChargeRefunds|distilled.Null A list of refunds that have been applied to the charge.
---@field review stripe.ChargeReview|distilled.Null ID of the review associated with this charge if one exists.
---@field shipping stripe.Shipping|distilled.Null Shipping information for the charge.
---@field source stripe.PaymentSource|distilled.Null This is a legacy field that will be removed in the future. It contains the Source, Card, or BankAccount object used for the charge. For details about the payment method used for this charge, refer to `payment_method` or `payment_method_details` instead.
---@field source_transfer stripe.ChargeSourceTransfer|distilled.Null The transfer ID which created this charge. Only present if the charge came from another Stripe account. [See the Connect documentation](https://docs.stripe.com/connect/destination-charges) for details.
---@field statement_descriptor string|distilled.Null For a non-card charge, text that appears on the customer's statement as the statement descriptor. This value overrides the account's default statement descriptor. For information about requirements, including the 22-character limit, see [the Statement Descriptor docs](https://docs.stripe.com/get-started/account/statement-descriptors). For a card charge, this value is ignored unless you don't specify a `statement_descriptor_suffix`, in which case this value is used as the suffix.
---@field statement_descriptor_suffix string|distilled.Null Provides information about a card charge. Concatenated to the account's [statement descriptor prefix](https://docs.stripe.com/get-started/account/statement-descriptors#static) to form the complete statement descriptor that appears on the customer's statement. If the account has no prefix value, the suffix is concatenated to the account's statement descriptor.
---@field status stripe.ChargeStatus The status of the payment is either `succeeded`, `pending`, or `failed`.
---@field transfer? stripe.ChargeTransfer ID of the transfer to the `destination` account (only applicable if the charge was created using the `destination` parameter).
---@field transfer_data stripe.ChargeTransferData|distilled.Null An optional dictionary including the account to automatically transfer to as part of a destination charge. [See the Connect documentation](https://docs.stripe.com/connect/destination-charges) for details.
---@field transfer_group string|distilled.Null A string that identifies this transaction as part of a group. See the [Connect documentation](https://docs.stripe.com/connect/separate-charges-and-transfers#transfer-options) for details.

---ID of the Connect application that created the charge.
---@alias stripe.ChargeApplication string|stripe.Application

---The application fee (if any) for the charge. [See the Connect documentation](https://docs.stripe.com/connect/direct-charges#collect-fees) for details.
---@alias stripe.ChargeApplicationFee string|stripe.ApplicationFee

---ID of the balance transaction that describes the impact of this charge on your account balance (not including refunds or disputes).
---@alias stripe.ChargeBalanceTransaction string|stripe.BalanceTransaction

---ID of the customer this charge is for if one exists.
---@alias stripe.ChargeCustomer string|stripe.Customer|stripe.DeletedCustomer

---ID of the balance transaction that describes the reversal of the balance on your account due to payment failure.
---@alias stripe.ChargeFailureBalanceTransaction string|stripe.BalanceTransaction

