---A Checkout Session represents your customer's session as they pay for
---one-time purchases or subscriptions through [Checkout](https://docs.stripe.com/payments/checkout)
---or [Payment Links](https://docs.stripe.com/payments/payment-links). We recommend creating a
---new Session each time your customer attempts to pay.
---
---Once payment is successful, the Checkout Session will contain a reference
---to the [Customer](https://docs.stripe.com/api/customers), and either the successful
---[PaymentIntent](https://docs.stripe.com/api/payment_intents) or an active
---[Subscription](https://docs.stripe.com/api/subscriptions).
---
---You can create a Checkout Session on your server and redirect to its URL
---to begin Checkout.
---
---Related guide: [Checkout quickstart](https://docs.stripe.com/checkout/quickstart)
---@class stripe.CheckoutSession
---@field adaptive_pricing stripe.PaymentPagesCheckoutSessionAdaptivePricing|distilled.Null Settings for price localization with [Adaptive Pricing](https://docs.stripe.com/payments/checkout/adaptive-pricing).
---@field after_expiration stripe.PaymentPagesCheckoutSessionAfterExpiration|distilled.Null When set, provides configuration for actions to take if this Checkout Session expires.
---@field allow_promotion_codes boolean|distilled.Null Enables user redeemable promotion codes.
---@field allowed_payment_method_types stripe.CheckoutSessionAllowedPaymentMethodTypesList|distilled.Null A list of the types of payment methods (e.g., `card`) this Checkout Session can accept.
---@field amount_subtotal number|distilled.Null Total of all items before discounts or taxes are applied.
---@field amount_total number|distilled.Null Total of all items after discounts and taxes are applied.
---@field automatic_tax stripe.PaymentPagesCheckoutSessionAutomaticTax
---@field billing_address_collection stripe.CheckoutSessionBillingAddressCollection|distilled.Null Describes whether Checkout should collect the customer's billing address. Defaults to `auto`.
---@field branding_settings? stripe.PaymentPagesCheckoutSessionBrandingSettings
---@field cancel_url string|distilled.Null If set, Checkout displays a back button and customers will be directed to this URL if they decide to cancel payment and return to your website.
---@field client_reference_id string|distilled.Null A unique string to reference the Checkout Session. This can be a customer ID, a cart ID, or similar, and can be used to reconcile the Session with your internal systems.
---@field client_secret distilled.Secret|distilled.Null The client secret of your Checkout Session. Applies to Checkout Sessions with `ui_mode: embedded_page` or `ui_mode: elements`. For `ui_mode: embedded_page`, the client secret is to be used when initializing Stripe.js embedded checkout. For `ui_mode: elements`, use the client secret with [initCheckout](https://docs.stripe.com/js/custom_checkout/init) on your front end.
---@field collected_information stripe.PaymentPagesCheckoutSessionCollectedInformation|distilled.Null Information about the customer collected within the Checkout Session.
---@field consent stripe.PaymentPagesCheckoutSessionConsent|distilled.Null Results of `consent_collection` for this session.
---@field consent_collection stripe.PaymentPagesCheckoutSessionConsentCollection|distilled.Null When set, provides configuration for the Checkout Session to gather active consent from customers.
---@field created number Time at which the object was created. Measured in seconds since the Unix epoch.
---@field currency string|distilled.Null Three-letter [ISO currency code](https://www.iso.org/iso-4217-currency-codes.html), in lowercase. Must be a [supported currency](https://stripe.com/docs/currencies).
---@field currency_conversion stripe.PaymentPagesCheckoutSessionCurrencyConversion|distilled.Null Currency conversion details for [Adaptive Pricing](https://docs.stripe.com/payments/checkout/adaptive-pricing) sessions created before 2025-03-31.
---@field custom_fields stripe.CheckoutSessionCustomFieldsList Collect additional information from your customer using custom fields. Up to 3 fields are supported. You can't set this parameter if `ui_mode` is `elements`.
---@field custom_text stripe.PaymentPagesCheckoutSessionCustomText
---@field customer stripe.CheckoutSessionCustomer|distilled.Null The ID of the customer for this Session. For Checkout Sessions in `subscription` mode or Checkout Sessions with `customer_creation` set as `always` in `payment` mode, Checkout will create a new customer object based on information provided during the payment flow unless an existing customer was provided when the Session was created.
---@field customer_account string|distilled.Null The ID of the account for this Session.
---@field customer_creation stripe.CheckoutSessionCustomerCreation|distilled.Null Configure whether a Checkout Session creates a Customer when the Checkout Session completes.
---@field customer_details stripe.PaymentPagesCheckoutSessionCustomerDetails|distilled.Null The customer details including the customer's tax exempt status and the customer's tax IDs. Customer's address details are not present on Sessions in `setup` mode.
---@field customer_email string|distilled.Null If provided, this value will be used when the Customer object is created. If not provided, customers will be asked to enter their email address. Use this parameter to prefill customer data if you already have an email on file. To access information about the customer once the payment flow is complete, use the `customer` attribute.
---@field discounts stripe.CheckoutSessionDiscountsList|distilled.Null List of coupons and promotion codes attached to the Checkout Session.
---@field excluded_payment_method_types? stripe.CheckoutSessionExcludedPaymentMethodTypesList A list of the types of payment methods (e.g., `card`) that should be excluded from this Checkout Session. This should only be used when payment methods for this Checkout Session are managed through the [Stripe Dashboard](https://dashboard.stripe.com/settings/payment_methods).
---@field expires_at number The timestamp at which the Checkout Session will expire.
---@field id string Unique identifier for the object.
---@field integration_identifier string|distilled.Null The integration identifier for this Checkout Session. Multiple Checkout Sessions can have the same integration identifier.
---@field invoice stripe.CheckoutSessionInvoice|distilled.Null ID of the invoice created by the Checkout Session, if it exists.
---@field invoice_creation stripe.PaymentPagesCheckoutSessionInvoiceCreation|distilled.Null Details on the state of invoice creation for the Checkout Session.
---@field line_items? stripe.CheckoutSessionLineItems The line items purchased by the customer.
---@field livemode boolean If the object exists in live mode, the value is `true`. If the object exists in test mode, the value is `false`.
---@field locale stripe.CheckoutSessionLocale|distilled.Null The IETF language tag of the locale Checkout is displayed in. If blank or `auto`, the browser's locale is used.
---@field managed_payments stripe.PaymentPagesCheckoutSessionManagedPayments|distilled.Null Settings for Managed Payments for this Checkout Session and resulting [PaymentIntents](/api/payment_intents/object), [Invoices](/api/invoices/object), and [Subscriptions](/api/subscriptions/object).
---@field metadata stripe.CheckoutSessionMetadataMap|distilled.Null Set of [key-value pairs](https://docs.stripe.com/api/metadata) that you can attach to an object. This can be useful for storing additional information about the object in a structured format.
---@field mode stripe.CheckoutSessionMode The mode of the Checkout Session.
---@field name_collection? stripe.PaymentPagesCheckoutSessionNameCollection
---@field object stripe.CheckoutSessionObject String representing the object's type. Objects of the same type share the same value.
---@field optional_items? stripe.CheckoutSessionOptionalItemsList|distilled.Null The optional items presented to the customer at checkout.
---@field origin_context stripe.CheckoutSessionOriginContext|distilled.Null Where the user is coming from. This informs the optimizations that are applied to the session.
---@field payment_intent stripe.CheckoutSessionPaymentIntent|distilled.Null The ID of the PaymentIntent for Checkout Sessions in `payment` mode. You can't confirm or cancel the PaymentIntent for a Checkout Session. To cancel, [expire the Checkout Session](https://docs.stripe.com/api/checkout/sessions/expire) instead.
---@field payment_link stripe.CheckoutSessionPaymentLink|distilled.Null The ID of the Payment Link that created this Session.
---@field payment_method_collection stripe.CheckoutSessionPaymentMethodCollection|distilled.Null Configure whether a Checkout Session should collect a payment method. Can only be set in `subscription` mode. Defaults to `always`.
---@field payment_method_configuration_details stripe.PaymentMethodConfigBizPaymentMethodConfigurationDetails|distilled.Null Information about the payment method configuration used for this Checkout session if using dynamic payment methods.
---@field payment_method_options stripe.CheckoutSessionPaymentMethodOptions|distilled.Null Payment-method-specific configuration for the PaymentIntent or SetupIntent of this CheckoutSession.
---@field payment_method_types stripe.CheckoutSessionPaymentMethodTypesList A list of the types of payment methods (e.g. card) this Checkout Session is allowed to accept.
---@field payment_status stripe.CheckoutSessionPaymentStatus The payment status of the Checkout Session, one of `paid`, `unpaid`, or `no_payment_required`. You can use this value to decide when to fulfill your customer's order.
---@field permissions stripe.PaymentPagesCheckoutSessionPermissions|distilled.Null This property is used to set up permissions for various actions (e.g., update) on the CheckoutSession object. For specific permissions, please refer to their dedicated subsections, such as `permissions.update_shipping_details`.
---@field phone_number_collection? stripe.PaymentPagesCheckoutSessionPhoneNumberCollection
---@field presentment_details? stripe.PaymentFlowsPaymentIntentPresentmentDetails
---@field recovered_from string|distilled.Null The ID of the original expired Checkout Session that triggered the recovery flow.
---@field redirect_on_completion? stripe.CheckoutSessionRedirectOnCompletion This parameter applies to `ui_mode: embedded_page`. Learn more about the [redirect behavior](https://docs.stripe.com/payments/checkout/custom-success-page?payment-ui=embedded-form) of embedded sessions. Defaults to `always`.
---@field return_url? string Applies to Checkout Sessions with `ui_mode: embedded_page` or `ui_mode: elements`. The URL to redirect your customer back to after they authenticate or cancel their payment on the payment method's app or site.
---@field saved_payment_method_options stripe.PaymentPagesCheckoutSessionSavedPaymentMethodOptions|distilled.Null Controls saved payment method settings for the session. Only available in `payment` and `subscription` mode.
---@field setup_intent stripe.CheckoutSessionSetupIntent|distilled.Null The ID of the SetupIntent for Checkout Sessions in `setup` mode. You can't confirm or cancel the SetupIntent for a Checkout Session. To cancel, [expire the Checkout Session](https://docs.stripe.com/api/checkout/sessions/expire) instead.
---@field shipping_address_collection stripe.PaymentPagesCheckoutSessionShippingAddressCollection|distilled.Null When set, provides configuration for Checkout to collect a shipping address from a customer.
---@field shipping_cost stripe.PaymentPagesCheckoutSessionShippingCost|distilled.Null The details of the customer cost of shipping, including the customer chosen ShippingRate.
---@field shipping_options stripe.CheckoutSessionShippingOptionsList The shipping rate options applied to this Session.
---@field status stripe.CheckoutSessionStatus|distilled.Null The status of the Checkout Session, one of `open`, `complete`, or `expired`.
---@field submit_type stripe.CheckoutSessionSubmitType|distilled.Null Describes the type of transaction being performed by Checkout in order to customize relevant text on the page, such as the submit button. `submit_type` can only be specified on Checkout Sessions in `payment` mode. If blank or `auto`, `pay` is used.
---@field subscription stripe.CheckoutSessionSubscription|distilled.Null The ID of the [Subscription](https://docs.stripe.com/api/subscriptions) for Checkout Sessions in `subscription` mode.
---@field success_url string|distilled.Null The URL the customer will be directed to after the payment or subscription creation is successful.
---@field tax_id_collection? stripe.PaymentPagesCheckoutSessionTaxIdCollection
---@field total_details stripe.PaymentPagesCheckoutSessionTotalDetails|distilled.Null Tax and discount details for the computed total amount.
---@field ui_mode stripe.CheckoutSessionUiMode|distilled.Null The UI mode of the Session. Defaults to `hosted_page`.
---@field url string|distilled.Null The URL to the Checkout Session. Applies to Checkout Sessions with `ui_mode: hosted_page`. Redirect customers to this URL to take them to Checkout. If you’re using [Custom Domains](https://docs.stripe.com/payments/checkout/custom-domains), the URL will use your subdomain. Otherwise, it’ll use `checkout.stripe.com.` This value is only present when the session is active.
---@field wallet_options stripe.CheckoutSessionWalletOptions|distilled.Null Wallet-specific configuration for this Checkout Session.

