---Orders represent your intent to purchase a particular Climate product. When you create an order, the
---payment is deducted from your merchant balance.
---@class stripe.ClimateOrder
---@field amount_fees number Total amount of [Frontier](https://frontierclimate.com/)'s service fees in the currency's smallest unit.
---@field amount_subtotal number Total amount of the carbon removal in the currency's smallest unit.
---@field amount_total number Total amount of the order including fees in the currency's smallest unit.
---@field beneficiary? stripe.ClimateRemovalsBeneficiary
---@field canceled_at number|distilled.Null Time at which the order was canceled. Measured in seconds since the Unix epoch.
---@field cancellation_reason stripe.ClimateOrderCancellationReason|distilled.Null Reason for the cancellation of this order.
---@field certificate string|distilled.Null For delivered orders, a URL to a delivery certificate for the order.
---@field confirmed_at number|distilled.Null Time at which the order was confirmed. Measured in seconds since the Unix epoch.
---@field created number Time at which the object was created. Measured in seconds since the Unix epoch.
---@field currency string Three-letter [ISO currency code](https://www.iso.org/iso-4217-currency-codes.html), in lowercase, representing the currency for this order.
---@field delayed_at number|distilled.Null Time at which the order's expected_delivery_year was delayed. Measured in seconds since the Unix epoch.
---@field delivered_at number|distilled.Null Time at which the order was delivered. Measured in seconds since the Unix epoch.
---@field delivery_details stripe.ClimateOrderDeliveryDetailsList Details about the delivery of carbon removal for this order.
---@field expected_delivery_year number The year this order is expected to be delivered. If the year is in the past, the order is a spot purchase and will be delivered within 30 days of purchase.
---@field id string Unique identifier for the object.
---@field livemode boolean Has the value `true` if the object exists in live mode or the value `false` if the object exists in test mode.
---@field metadata stripe.ClimateOrderMetadataMap Set of [key-value pairs](https://docs.stripe.com/api/metadata) that you can attach to an object. This can be useful for storing additional information about the object in a structured format.
---@field metric_tons string Quantity of carbon removal that is included in this order.
---@field object stripe.ClimateOrderObject String representing the object's type. Objects of the same type share the same value.
---@field product stripe.ClimateOrderProduct Unique ID for the Climate `Product` this order is purchasing.
---@field product_substituted_at number|distilled.Null Time at which the order's product was substituted for a different product. Measured in seconds since the Unix epoch.
---@field status stripe.ClimateOrderStatus The current status of this order.

---Reason for the cancellation of this order.
---@alias stripe.ClimateOrderCancellationReason "expired"|"product_unavailable"|"requested"

---Details about the delivery of carbon removal for this order.
---@alias stripe.ClimateOrderDeliveryDetailsList stripe.ClimateRemovalsOrderDeliveries[]

---Set of [key-value pairs](https://docs.stripe.com/api/metadata) that you can attach to an object. This can be useful for storing additional information about the object in a structured format.
---@alias stripe.ClimateOrderMetadataMap { [string]: string }

---String representing the object's type. Objects of the same type share the same value.
---@alias stripe.ClimateOrderObject "climate.order"

---Unique ID for the Climate `Product` this order is purchasing.
---@alias stripe.ClimateOrderProduct string|stripe.ClimateProduct

---The current status of this order.
---@alias stripe.ClimateOrderStatus "awaiting_funds"|"canceled"|"confirmed"|"delivered"|"open"

---A Climate product represents a type of carbon removal unit available for reservation.
---You can retrieve it to see the current price and availability.
---@class stripe.ClimateProduct
---@field created number Time at which the object was created. Measured in seconds since the Unix epoch.
---@field current_prices_per_metric_ton stripe.ClimateProductCurrentPricesPerMetricTonMap Current prices for a metric ton of carbon removal in a currency's smallest unit.
---@field delivery_year number|distilled.Null The year in which the carbon removal is expected to be delivered. If the year is in the past, this represents spot inventory with guaranteed delivery.
---@field id string Unique identifier for the object. For convenience, Climate product IDs are human-readable strings that start with `climsku_`. See [carbon removal inventory](https://stripe.com/docs/climate/orders/carbon-removal-inventory) for a list of available carbon removal products.
---@field livemode boolean Has the value `true` if the object exists in live mode or the value `false` if the object exists in test mode.
---@field metric_tons_available string The quantity of metric tons available for reservation.
---@field name string The Climate product's name.
---@field object stripe.ClimateProductObject String representing the object's type. Objects of the same type share the same value.
---@field suppliers stripe.ClimateProductSuppliersList The carbon removal suppliers that fulfill orders for this Climate product.

---Current prices for a metric ton of carbon removal in a currency's smallest unit.
---@alias stripe.ClimateProductCurrentPricesPerMetricTonMap { [string]: stripe.ClimateRemovalsProductsPrice }

---String representing the object's type. Objects of the same type share the same value.
---@alias stripe.ClimateProductObject "climate.product"

---The carbon removal suppliers that fulfill orders for this Climate product.
---@alias stripe.ClimateProductSuppliersList stripe.ClimateSupplier[]

---@class stripe.ClimateRemovalsBeneficiary
---@field public_name string Publicly displayable name for the end beneficiary of carbon removal.

---@class stripe.ClimateRemovalsLocation
---@field city string|distilled.Null The city where the supplier is located.
---@field country string Two-letter ISO code representing the country where the supplier is located.
---@field latitude number|distilled.Null The geographic latitude where the supplier is located.
---@field longitude number|distilled.Null The geographic longitude where the supplier is located.
---@field region string|distilled.Null The state/county/province/region where the supplier is located.

---The delivery of a specified quantity of carbon for an order.
---@class stripe.ClimateRemovalsOrderDeliveries
---@field delivered_at number Time at which the delivery occurred. Measured in seconds since the Unix epoch.
---@field location stripe.ClimateRemovalsLocation|distilled.Null Specific location of this delivery.
---@field metric_tons string Quantity of carbon removal supplied by this delivery.
---@field registry_url string|distilled.Null Once retired, a URL to the registry entry for the tons from this delivery.
---@field supplier stripe.ClimateSupplier

---@class stripe.ClimateRemovalsProductsPrice
---@field amount_fees number Fees for one metric ton of carbon removal in the currency's smallest unit.
---@field amount_subtotal number Subtotal for one metric ton of carbon removal (excluding fees) in the currency's smallest unit.
---@field amount_total number Total for one metric ton of carbon removal (including fees) in the currency's smallest unit.

---A supplier of carbon removal.
---@class stripe.ClimateSupplier
---@field id string Unique identifier for the object.
---@field info_url string Link to a webpage to learn more about the supplier.
---@field livemode boolean Has the value `true` if the object exists in live mode or the value `false` if the object exists in test mode.
---@field locations stripe.ClimateSupplierLocationsList The locations in which this supplier operates.
---@field name string Name of this carbon removal supplier.
---@field object stripe.ClimateSupplierObject String representing the object’s type. Objects of the same type share the same value.
---@field removal_pathway stripe.ClimateSupplierRemovalPathway The scientific pathway used for carbon removal.

---The locations in which this supplier operates.
---@alias stripe.ClimateSupplierLocationsList stripe.ClimateRemovalsLocation[]

---String representing the object’s type. Objects of the same type share the same value.
---@alias stripe.ClimateSupplierObject "climate.supplier"

---The scientific pathway used for carbon removal.
---@alias stripe.ClimateSupplierRemovalPathway "biomass_carbon_removal_and_storage"|"direct_air_capture"|"enhanced_weathering"|"marine_carbon_removal"

---ConfirmationTokens help transport client side data collected by Stripe JS over
---to your server for confirming a PaymentIntent or SetupIntent. If the confirmation
---is successful, values present on the ConfirmationToken are written onto the Intent.
---
---To learn more about how to use ConfirmationToken, visit the related guides:
---- [Finalize payments on the server](https://docs.stripe.com/payments/finalize-payments-on-the-server)
---- [Build two-step confirmation](https://docs.stripe.com/payments/build-a-two-step-confirmation).
---@class stripe.ConfirmationToken
---@field created number Time at which the object was created. Measured in seconds since the Unix epoch.
---@field expires_at number|distilled.Null Time at which this ConfirmationToken expires and can no longer be used to confirm a PaymentIntent or SetupIntent.
---@field id string Unique identifier for the object.
---@field livemode boolean If the object exists in live mode, the value is `true`. If the object exists in test mode, the value is `false`.
---@field mandate_data? stripe.ConfirmationTokensResourceMandateData|distilled.Null Data used for generating a Mandate.
---@field metadata stripe.ConfirmationTokenMetadataMap|distilled.Null Set of key-value pairs that you can attach to an object. This can be useful for storing additional information about the object in a structured format.
---@field object stripe.ConfirmationTokenObject String representing the object's type. Objects of the same type share the same value.
---@field payment_intent string|distilled.Null ID of the PaymentIntent that this ConfirmationToken was used to confirm, or null if this ConfirmationToken has not yet been used.
---@field payment_method_options stripe.ConfirmationTokensResourcePaymentMethodOptions|distilled.Null Payment-method-specific configuration for this ConfirmationToken.
---@field payment_method_preview stripe.ConfirmationTokensResourcePaymentMethodPreview|distilled.Null Payment details collected by the Payment Element, used to create a PaymentMethod when a PaymentIntent or SetupIntent is confirmed with this ConfirmationToken.
---@field return_url string|distilled.Null Return URL used to confirm the Intent.
---@field setup_future_usage stripe.ConfirmationTokenSetupFutureUsage|distilled.Null Indicates that you intend to make future payments with this ConfirmationToken's payment method. The presence of this property will [attach the payment method](https://docs.stripe.com/payments/save-during-payment) to the PaymentIntent's Customer, if present, after the PaymentIntent is confirmed and any required actions from the user are complete.
---@field setup_intent string|distilled.Null ID of the SetupIntent that this ConfirmationToken was used to confirm, or null if this ConfirmationToken has not yet been used.
---@field shipping stripe.ConfirmationTokensResourceShipping|distilled.Null Shipping information collected on this ConfirmationToken.
---@field use_stripe_sdk boolean Indicates whether the Stripe SDK is used to handle confirmation flow. Defaults to `true` on ConfirmationToken.

---Set of key-value pairs that you can attach to an object. This can be useful for storing additional information about the object in a structured format.
---@alias stripe.ConfirmationTokenMetadataMap { [string]: string }

---String representing the object's type. Objects of the same type share the same value.
---@alias stripe.ConfirmationTokenObject "confirmation_token"

---Indicates that you intend to make future payments with this ConfirmationToken's payment method.
---
---The presence of this property will [attach the payment method](https://docs.stripe.com/payments/save-during-payment) to the PaymentIntent's Customer, if present, after the PaymentIntent is confirmed and any required actions from the user are complete.
---@alias stripe.ConfirmationTokenSetupFutureUsage "off_session"|"on_session"

