---A subset of parameters to be passed to subscription creation for Checkout Sessions in `subscription` mode.
---@class stripe.CreateCheckoutSessionRequestSubscriptionData
---@field application_fee_percent? number A non-negative decimal between 0 and 100, with at most two decimal places. This represents the percentage of the subscription invoice total that will be transferred to the application owner's Stripe account. To use an application fee percent, the request must be made on behalf of another account, using the `Stripe-Account` header or an OAuth key. For more information, see the application fees [documentation](https://stripe.com/docs/connect/subscriptions#collecting-fees-on-subscriptions).
---@field billing_cycle_anchor? number A future timestamp to anchor the subscription's billing cycle for new subscriptions.
---@field billing_cycle_anchor_config? stripe.CreateCheckoutSessionRequestSubscriptionDataBillingCycleAnchorConfig Configures when the subscription schedule's billing cycle anchors to a specific day of the week or month.
---@field billing_mode? stripe.CreateCheckoutSessionRequestSubscriptionDataBillingMode Controls how prorations and invoices for subscriptions are calculated and orchestrated.
---@field default_tax_rates? stripe.CreateCheckoutSessionRequestSubscriptionDataDefaultTaxRatesList The tax rates that will apply to any subscription item that does not have `tax_rates` set. Invoices created will have their `default_tax_rates` populated from the subscription.
---@field description? string The subscription's description, meant to be displayable to the customer. Use this field to optionally store an explanation of the subscription for rendering in the [customer portal](https://docs.stripe.com/customer-management).
---@field invoice_settings? stripe.CreateCheckoutSessionRequestSubscriptionDataInvoiceSettings All invoices will be billed using the specified settings.
---@field metadata? stripe.CreateCheckoutSessionRequestSubscriptionDataMetadataMap Set of [key-value pairs](https://docs.stripe.com/api/metadata) that you can attach to an object. This can be useful for storing additional information about the object in a structured format. Individual keys can be unset by posting an empty value to them. All keys can be unset by posting an empty value to `metadata`.
---@field on_behalf_of? string The account on behalf of which to charge, for each of the subscription's invoices.
---@field pending_invoice_item_interval? stripe.CreateCheckoutSessionRequestSubscriptionDataPendingInvoiceItemInterval Specifies an interval for how often to bill for any pending invoice items. It is analogous to calling [Create an invoice](https://docs.stripe.com/api#create_invoice) for the given subscription at the specified interval.
---@field proration_behavior? stripe.CreateCheckoutSessionRequestSubscriptionDataProrationBehavior|string Determines how to handle prorations resulting from the `billing_cycle_anchor`. If no value is passed, the default is `create_prorations`.
---@field transfer_data? stripe.CreateCheckoutSessionRequestSubscriptionDataTransferData If specified, the funds from the subscription's invoices will be transferred to the destination and the ID of the resulting transfers will be found on the resulting charges.
---@field trial_end? number Unix timestamp representing the end of the trial period the customer will get before being charged for the first time. Has to be at least 48 hours in the future.
---@field trial_period_days? number Integer representing the number of trial period days before the customer is charged for the first time. Has to be at least 1.
---@field trial_settings? stripe.CreateCheckoutSessionRequestSubscriptionDataTrialSettings Settings related to subscription trials.

