---@class stripe.CreateCoreAccountRequest
---@field account_token? string The account token generated by the account token API.
---@field configuration? stripe.CreateCoreAccountRequestConfiguration An Account Configuration which allows the Account to take on a key persona across Stripe products.
---@field contact_email? string The primary contact email address for the Account.
---@field contact_phone? string The default contact phone for the Account.
---@field dashboard? stripe.CreateCoreAccountRequestDashboard|string A value indicating the Stripe dashboard this Account has access to. This will depend on which configurations are enabled for this account.
---@field defaults? stripe.CreateCoreAccountRequestDefaults Default values to be used on Account Configurations.
---@field display_name? string A descriptive name for the Account. This name will be surfaced in the Stripe Dashboard and on any invoices sent to the Account.
---@field identity? stripe.CreateCoreAccountRequestIdentity Information about the company, individual, and business represented by the Account.
---@field include? stripe.CreateCoreAccountRequestIncludeList Additional fields to include in the response.
---@field metadata? stripe.CreateCoreAccountRequestMetadataMap Set of key-value pairs that you can attach to an object. This can be useful for storing additional information about the object in a structured format.
---@field idempotencyKey? string A unique key (up to 255 characters, for example a V4 UUID) that makes a retry of this request safe: Stripe returns the first result for a repeated key instead of performing the operation twice. See https://docs.stripe.com/api/idempotent_requests.

---An Account Configuration which allows the Account to take on a key persona across Stripe products.
---@class stripe.CreateCoreAccountRequestConfiguration
---@field customer? stripe.CreateCoreAccountRequestConfigurationCustomer The Customer Configuration allows the Account to be used in inbound payment flows (i.e. customer-facing payment and billing flows).
---@field merchant? stripe.CreateCoreAccountRequestConfigurationMerchant Enables the Account to act as a connected account and collect payments facilitated by a Connect platform. You must onboard your platform to Connect before you can add this configuration to your connected accounts. Utilize this configuration when the Account will be the Merchant of Record, like with Direct charges or Destination Charges with on_behalf_of set.
---@field recipient? stripe.CreateCoreAccountRequestConfigurationRecipient The Recipient Configuration allows the Account to receive funds. Utilize this configuration if the Account will not be the Merchant of Record, like with Separate Charges & Transfers, or Destination Charges without on_behalf_of set.

---The Customer Configuration allows the Account to be used in inbound payment flows (i.e. customer-facing payment and billing flows).
---@class stripe.CreateCoreAccountRequestConfigurationCustomer
---@field automatic_indirect_tax? stripe.CreateCoreAccountRequestConfigurationCustomerAutomaticIndirectTax Automatic indirect tax settings to be used when automatic tax calculation is enabled on the customer's invoices, subscriptions, checkout sessions, or payment links. Surfaces if automatic tax calculation is possible given the current customer location information.
---@field billing? stripe.CreateCoreAccountRequestConfigurationCustomerBilling Billing settings - default settings used for this customer in Billing flows such as Invoices and Subscriptions.
---@field capabilities? stripe.CreateCoreAccountRequestConfigurationCustomerCapabilities Capabilities that have been requested on the Customer Configuration.
---@field shipping? stripe.CreateCoreAccountRequestConfigurationCustomerShipping The customer's shipping information. Appears on invoices emailed to this customer.
---@field test_clock? string ID of the test clock to attach to the customer. Can only be set on testmode Accounts, and when the Customer Configuration is first set on an Account.

---Automatic indirect tax settings to be used when automatic tax calculation is enabled on the customer's invoices, subscriptions, checkout sessions, or payment links. Surfaces if automatic tax calculation is possible given the current customer location information.
---@class stripe.CreateCoreAccountRequestConfigurationCustomerAutomaticIndirectTax
---@field exempt? stripe.CreateCoreAccountRequestConfigurationCustomerAutomaticIndirectTaxExempt|string Describes the customer's tax exemption status, which is `none`, `exempt`, or `reverse`. When set to reverse, invoice and receipt PDFs include the following text: "Reverse charge".
---@field ip_address? string A recent IP address of the customer used for tax reporting and tax location inference.

---Describes the customer's tax exemption status, which is `none`, `exempt`, or `reverse`. When set to reverse, invoice and receipt PDFs include the following text: "Reverse charge".
---@alias stripe.CreateCoreAccountRequestConfigurationCustomerAutomaticIndirectTaxExempt "exempt"|"none"|"reverse"

---Billing settings - default settings used for this customer in Billing flows such as Invoices and Subscriptions.
---@class stripe.CreateCoreAccountRequestConfigurationCustomerBilling
---@field invoice? stripe.CreateCoreAccountRequestConfigurationCustomerBillingInvoice Default invoice settings for the customer account.

---Default invoice settings for the customer account.
---@class stripe.CreateCoreAccountRequestConfigurationCustomerBillingInvoice
---@field custom_fields? stripe.CreateCoreAccountRequestConfigurationCustomerBillingInvoiceCustomFieldsList The list of up to 4 default custom fields to be displayed on invoices for this customer.
---@field footer? string Default invoice footer.
---@field next_sequence? number Sequence number to use on the customer account's next invoice. Defaults to 1.
---@field prefix? string Prefix used to generate unique invoice numbers. Must be 3-12 uppercase letters or numbers.
---@field rendering? stripe.CreateCoreAccountRequestConfigurationCustomerBillingInvoiceRendering Default invoice PDF rendering options.

---@class stripe.CreateCoreAccountRequestConfigurationCustomerBillingInvoiceCustomFieldsItem
---@field name string The name of the custom field. This may be up to 40 characters.
---@field value string The value of the custom field. This may be up to 140 characters. When updating, pass an empty string to remove previously-defined values.

---The list of up to 4 default custom fields to be displayed on invoices for this customer.
---@alias stripe.CreateCoreAccountRequestConfigurationCustomerBillingInvoiceCustomFieldsList stripe.CreateCoreAccountRequestConfigurationCustomerBillingInvoiceCustomFieldsItem[]

---Default invoice PDF rendering options.
---@class stripe.CreateCoreAccountRequestConfigurationCustomerBillingInvoiceRendering
---@field amount_tax_display? stripe.CreateCoreAccountRequestConfigurationCustomerBillingInvoiceRenderingAmountTaxDisplay|string Indicates whether displayed line item prices and amounts on invoice PDFs include inclusive tax amounts. Must be either `include_inclusive_tax` or `exclude_tax`.
---@field template? string ID of the invoice rendering template to use for future invoices.

---Indicates whether displayed line item prices and amounts on invoice PDFs include inclusive tax amounts. Must be either `include_inclusive_tax` or `exclude_tax`.
