---@class stripe.CreateInvoiceitemRequest
---@field amount? number The integer amount in cents (or local equivalent) of the charge to be applied to the upcoming invoice. Passing in a negative `amount` will reduce the `amount_due` on the invoice.
---@field currency? string Three-letter [ISO currency code](https://www.iso.org/iso-4217-currency-codes.html), in lowercase. Must be a [supported currency](https://stripe.com/docs/currencies).
---@field customer? string The ID of the customer to bill for this invoice item.
---@field customer_account? string The ID of the account representing the customer to bill for this invoice item.
---@field description? string An arbitrary string which you can attach to the invoice item. The description is displayed in the invoice for easy tracking.
---@field discountable? boolean Controls whether discounts apply to this invoice item. Defaults to false for prorations or negative invoice items, and true for all other invoice items.
---@field discounts? stripe.CreateInvoiceitemRequestDiscounts The coupons and promotion codes to redeem into discounts for the invoice item or invoice line item.
---@field expand? stripe.CreateInvoiceitemRequestExpandList Specifies which fields in the response should be expanded.
---@field invoice? string The ID of an existing invoice to add this invoice item to. For subscription invoices, when left blank, the invoice item will be added to the next upcoming scheduled invoice. For standalone invoices, the invoice item won't be automatically added unless you pass `pending_invoice_item_behavior: 'include'` when creating the invoice. This is useful when adding invoice items in response to an invoice.created webhook. You can only add invoice items to draft invoices and there is a maximum of 250 items per invoice.
---@field metadata? stripe.CreateInvoiceitemRequestMetadata Set of [key-value pairs](https://docs.stripe.com/api/metadata) that you can attach to an object. This can be useful for storing additional information about the object in a structured format. Individual keys can be unset by posting an empty value to them. All keys can be unset by posting an empty value to `metadata`.
---@field period? stripe.CreateInvoiceitemRequestPeriod The period associated with this invoice item. When set to different values, the period will be rendered on the invoice. If you have [Stripe Revenue Recognition](https://docs.stripe.com/revenue-recognition) enabled, the period will be used to recognize and defer revenue. See the [Revenue Recognition documentation](https://docs.stripe.com/revenue-recognition/methodology/subscriptions-and-invoicing) for details.
---@field price_data? stripe.CreateInvoiceitemRequestPriceData Data used to generate a new [Price](https://docs.stripe.com/api/prices) object inline.
---@field pricing? stripe.CreateInvoiceitemRequestPricing The pricing information for the invoice item.
---@field quantity? number Non-negative integer. The quantity of units for the invoice item. Use `quantity_decimal` instead to provide decimal precision. This field will be deprecated in favor of `quantity_decimal` in a future version.
---@field quantity_decimal? string Non-negative decimal with at most 12 decimal places. The quantity of units for the invoice item.
---@field subscription? string The ID of a subscription to add this invoice item to. When left blank, the invoice item is added to the next upcoming scheduled invoice. When set, scheduled invoices for subscriptions other than the specified subscription will ignore the invoice item. Use this when you want to express that an invoice item has been accrued within the context of a particular subscription.
---@field tax_behavior? stripe.CreateInvoiceitemRequestTaxBehavior|string Only required if a [default tax behavior](https://docs.stripe.com/tax/products-prices-tax-categories-tax-behavior#setting-a-default-tax-behavior-(recommended)) was not provided in the Stripe Tax settings. Specifies whether the price is considered inclusive of taxes or exclusive of taxes. One of `inclusive`, `exclusive`, or `unspecified`. Once specified as either `inclusive` or `exclusive`, it cannot be changed.
