---@class stripe.CreateIssuingCardRequest
---@field cardholder? string The [Cardholder](https://docs.stripe.com/api#issuing_cardholder_object) object with which the card will be associated.
---@field currency string The currency for the card.
---@field exp_month? number The desired expiration month (1-12) for this card if [specifying a custom expiration date](/issuing/cards/virtual/issue-cards?testing-method=with-code#exp-dates).
---@field exp_year? number The desired 4-digit expiration year for this card if [specifying a custom expiration date](/issuing/cards/virtual/issue-cards?testing-method=with-code#exp-dates).
---@field expand? stripe.CreateIssuingCardRequestExpandList Specifies which fields in the response should be expanded.
---@field financial_account? string The new financial account ID the card will be associated with. This field allows a card to be reassigned to a different financial account.
---@field lifecycle_controls? stripe.CreateIssuingCardRequestLifecycleControls Rules that control the lifecycle of this card, such as automatic cancellation. Refer to our [documentation](/issuing/controls/lifecycle-controls) for more details.
---@field metadata? stripe.CreateIssuingCardRequestMetadataMap Set of [key-value pairs](https://docs.stripe.com/api/metadata) that you can attach to an object. This can be useful for storing additional information about the object in a structured format. Individual keys can be unset by posting an empty value to them. All keys can be unset by posting an empty value to `metadata`.
---@field personalization_design? string The personalization design object belonging to this card.
---@field pin? stripe.CreateIssuingCardRequestPin The desired PIN for this card.
---@field replacement_for? string The card this is meant to be a replacement for (if any).
---@field replacement_reason? stripe.CreateIssuingCardRequestReplacementReason|string If `replacement_for` is specified, this should indicate why that card is being replaced.
---@field second_line? stripe.CreateIssuingCardRequestSecondLine The second line to print on the card. Max length: 24 characters.
---@field shipping? stripe.CreateIssuingCardRequestShipping The address where the card will be shipped.
---@field spending_controls? stripe.CreateIssuingCardRequestSpendingControls Rules that control spending for this card. Refer to our [documentation](https://docs.stripe.com/issuing/controls/spending-controls) for more details.
---@field status? stripe.CreateIssuingCardRequestStatus|string Whether authorizations can be approved on this card. May be blocked from activating cards depending on past-due Cardholder requirements. Defaults to `inactive`.
---@field type stripe.CreateIssuingCardRequestType|string The type of card to issue. Possible values are `physical` or `virtual`.
---@field idempotencyKey? string A unique key (up to 255 characters, for example a V4 UUID) that makes a retry of this request safe: Stripe returns the first result for a repeated key instead of performing the operation twice. See https://docs.stripe.com/api/idempotent_requests.

---Specifies which fields in the response should be expanded.
---@alias stripe.CreateIssuingCardRequestExpandList string[]

---Rules that control the lifecycle of this card, such as automatic cancellation. Refer to our [documentation](/issuing/controls/lifecycle-controls) for more details.
---@class stripe.CreateIssuingCardRequestLifecycleControls
---@field cancel_after stripe.CreateIssuingCardRequestLifecycleControlsCancelAfter Cancels the card after the specified conditions are met.

---Cancels the card after the specified conditions are met.
---@class stripe.CreateIssuingCardRequestLifecycleControlsCancelAfter
---@field payment_count number The card is automatically cancelled when it makes this number of non-zero payment authorizations and transactions. The count includes penny authorizations, but doesn't include non-payment actions, such as authorization advice.

