---@class stripe.CreateIssuingCardholderRequest
---@field billing stripe.CreateIssuingCardholderRequestBilling The cardholder's billing address.
---@field company? stripe.CreateIssuingCardholderRequestCompany Additional information about a `company` cardholder.
---@field email? string The cardholder's email address.
---@field expand? stripe.CreateIssuingCardholderRequestExpandList Specifies which fields in the response should be expanded.
---@field individual? stripe.CreateIssuingCardholderRequestIndividual Additional information about an `individual` cardholder.
---@field metadata? stripe.CreateIssuingCardholderRequestMetadataMap Set of [key-value pairs](https://docs.stripe.com/api/metadata) that you can attach to an object. This can be useful for storing additional information about the object in a structured format. Individual keys can be unset by posting an empty value to them. All keys can be unset by posting an empty value to `metadata`.
---@field name string The cardholder's name. This will be printed on cards issued to them. The maximum length of this field is 24 characters. This field cannot contain any special characters or numbers.
---@field phone_number? string The cardholder's phone number. This will be transformed to [E.164](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E.164) if it is not provided in that format already. This is required for all cardholders who will be creating EU cards. See the [3D Secure documentation](https://docs.stripe.com/issuing/3d-secure#when-is-3d-secure-applied) for more details.
---@field preferred_locales? stripe.CreateIssuingCardholderRequestPreferredLocalesList The cardholder’s preferred locales (languages), ordered by preference. Locales can be `de`, `en`, `es`, `fr`, or `it`. This changes the language of the [3D Secure flow](https://docs.stripe.com/issuing/3d-secure) and one-time password messages sent to the cardholder.
---@field spending_controls? stripe.CreateIssuingCardholderRequestSpendingControls Rules that control spending across this cardholder's cards. Refer to our [documentation](https://docs.stripe.com/issuing/controls/spending-controls) for more details.
---@field status? stripe.CreateIssuingCardholderRequestStatus|string Specifies whether to permit authorizations on this cardholder's cards. Defaults to `active`.
---@field type? stripe.CreateIssuingCardholderRequestType|string One of `individual` or `company`. See [Choose a cardholder type](https://docs.stripe.com/issuing/other/choose-cardholder) for more details.
---@field idempotencyKey? string A unique key (up to 255 characters, for example a V4 UUID) that makes a retry of this request safe: Stripe returns the first result for a repeated key instead of performing the operation twice. See https://docs.stripe.com/api/idempotent_requests.

---The cardholder's billing address.
---@class stripe.CreateIssuingCardholderRequestBilling
---@field address stripe.CreateIssuingCardholderRequestBillingAddress The cardholder’s billing address.

---The cardholder’s billing address.
---@class stripe.CreateIssuingCardholderRequestBillingAddress
---@field city string City, district, suburb, town, or village.
---@field country string Two-letter country code ([ISO 3166-1 alpha-2](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISO_3166-1_alpha-2)).
---@field line1 string Address line 1, such as the street, PO Box, or company name.
---@field line2? string Address line 2, such as the apartment, suite, unit, or building.
---@field postal_code string ZIP or postal code.
---@field state? string State, county, province, or region ([ISO 3166-2](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISO_3166-2)).

---Additional information about a `company` cardholder.
---@class stripe.CreateIssuingCardholderRequestCompany
---@field tax_id? string The entity's business ID number.

---Specifies which fields in the response should be expanded.
---@alias stripe.CreateIssuingCardholderRequestExpandList string[]

---Additional information about an `individual` cardholder.
---@class stripe.CreateIssuingCardholderRequestIndividual
---@field card_issuing? stripe.CreateIssuingCardholderRequestIndividualCardIssuing Information related to the card_issuing program for this cardholder.
---@field dob? stripe.CreateIssuingCardholderRequestIndividualDob The date of birth of this cardholder. Cardholders must be older than 13 years old.
---@field first_name? string The first name of this cardholder. Required before activating Cards. This field cannot contain any numbers, special characters (except periods, commas, hyphens, spaces and apostrophes) or non-latin letters.
---@field last_name? string The last name of this cardholder. Required before activating Cards. This field cannot contain any numbers, special characters (except periods, commas, hyphens, spaces and apostrophes) or non-latin letters.
---@field verification? stripe.CreateIssuingCardholderRequestIndividualVerification Government-issued ID document for this cardholder.

---Information related to the card_issuing program for this cardholder.
---@class stripe.CreateIssuingCardholderRequestIndividualCardIssuing
---@field user_terms_acceptance? stripe.CreateIssuingCardholderRequestIndividualCardIssuingUserTermsAcceptance Information about cardholder acceptance of Celtic [Authorized User Terms](https://docs.stripe.com/issuing/compliance-us#issuing-terms). Required for cards backed by a Celtic program.

---Information about cardholder acceptance of Celtic [Authorized User Terms](https://docs.stripe.com/issuing/compliance-us#issuing-terms). Required for cards backed by a Celtic program.
---@class stripe.CreateIssuingCardholderRequestIndividualCardIssuingUserTermsAcceptance
---@field date? number The Unix timestamp marking when the cardholder accepted the Authorized User Terms.
---@field ip? string The IP address from which the cardholder accepted the Authorized User Terms.
---@field user_agent? stripe.CreateIssuingCardholderRequestIndividualCardIssuingUserTermsAcceptanceUserAgent The user agent of the browser from which the cardholder accepted the Authorized User Terms.

---The user agent of the browser from which the cardholder accepted the Authorized User Terms.
---@alias stripe.CreateIssuingCardholderRequestIndividualCardIssuingUserTermsAcceptanceUserAgent string|stripe.CreateIssuingCardholderRequestIndividualCardIssuingUserTermsAcceptanceUserAgentCase1|string

---@alias stripe.CreateIssuingCardholderRequestIndividualCardIssuingUserTermsAcceptanceUserAgentCase1 ""

---The date of birth of this cardholder. Cardholders must be older than 13 years old.
---@class stripe.CreateIssuingCardholderRequestIndividualDob
---@field day number The day of birth, between 1 and 31.
---@field month number The month of birth, between 1 and 12.
---@field year number The four-digit year of birth.

---Government-issued ID document for this cardholder.
---@class stripe.CreateIssuingCardholderRequestIndividualVerification
---@field document? stripe.CreateIssuingCardholderRequestIndividualVerificationDocument An identifying document, either a passport or local ID card.

---An identifying document, either a passport or local ID card.
---@class stripe.CreateIssuingCardholderRequestIndividualVerificationDocument
---@field back? string The back of an ID returned by a [file upload](https://docs.stripe.com/api#create_file) with a `purpose` value of `identity_document`.
---@field front? string The front of an ID returned by a [file upload](https://docs.stripe.com/api#create_file) with a `purpose` value of `identity_document`.

---Set of [key-value pairs](https://docs.stripe.com/api/metadata) that you can attach to an object. This can be useful for storing additional information about the object in a structured format. Individual keys can be unset by posting an empty value to them. All keys can be unset by posting an empty value to `metadata`.
---@alias stripe.CreateIssuingCardholderRequestMetadataMap { [string]: string }

---@alias stripe.CreateIssuingCardholderRequestPreferredLocalesItem "de"|"en"|"es"|"fr"|"it"

---The cardholder’s preferred locales (languages), ordered by preference. Locales can be `de`, `en`, `es`, `fr`, or `it`.
--- This changes the language of the [3D Secure flow](https://docs.stripe.com/issuing/3d-secure) and one-time password messages sent to the cardholder.
---@alias stripe.CreateIssuingCardholderRequestPreferredLocalesList (stripe.CreateIssuingCardholderRequestPreferredLocalesItem|string)[]

---Rules that control spending across this cardholder's cards. Refer to our [documentation](https://docs.stripe.com/issuing/controls/spending-controls) for more details.
---@class stripe.CreateIssuingCardholderRequestSpendingControls
---@field allowed_card_presences? stripe.CreateIssuingCardholderRequestSpendingControlsAllowedCardPresencesList Array of card presence statuses from which authorizations will be allowed. Possible options are `present`, `not_present`. All other statuses will be blocked. Cannot be set with `blocked_card_presences`. Provide an empty value to unset this control.
---@field allowed_categories? stripe.CreateIssuingCardholderRequestSpendingControlsAllowedCategoriesList Array of strings containing [categories](https://docs.stripe.com/api#issuing_authorization_object-merchant_data-category) of authorizations to allow. All other categories will be blocked. Cannot be set with `blocked_categories`.
---@field allowed_merchant_countries? stripe.CreateIssuingCardholderRequestSpendingControlsAllowedMerchantCountriesList Array of strings containing representing countries from which authorizations will be allowed. Authorizations from merchants in all other countries will be declined. Country codes should be ISO 3166 alpha-2 country codes (e.g. `US`). Cannot be set with `blocked_merchant_countries`. Provide an empty value to unset this control.
---@field blocked_card_presences? stripe.CreateIssuingCardholderRequestSpendingControlsBlockedCardPresencesList Array of card presence statuses from which authorizations will be declined. Possible options are `present`, `not_present`. Cannot be set with `allowed_card_presences`. Provide an empty value to unset this control.
---@field blocked_categories? stripe.CreateIssuingCardholderRequestSpendingControlsBlockedCategoriesList Array of strings containing [categories](https://docs.stripe.com/api#issuing_authorization_object-merchant_data-category) of authorizations to decline. All other categories will be allowed. Cannot be set with `allowed_categories`.
---@field blocked_merchant_countries? stripe.CreateIssuingCardholderRequestSpendingControlsBlockedMerchantCountriesList Array of strings containing representing countries from which authorizations will be declined. Country codes should be ISO 3166 alpha-2 country codes (e.g. `US`). Cannot be set with `allowed_merchant_countries`. Provide an empty value to unset this control.
---@field spending_limits? stripe.CreateIssuingCardholderRequestSpendingControlsSpendingLimitsList Limit spending with amount-based rules that apply across this cardholder's cards.
---@field spending_limits_currency? string Currency of amounts within `spending_limits`. Defaults to your merchant country's currency.

---@alias stripe.CreateIssuingCardholderRequestSpendingControlsAllowedCardPresencesItem "not_present"|"present"

---Array of card presence statuses from which authorizations will be allowed. Possible options are `present`, `not_present`. All other statuses will be blocked. Cannot be set with `blocked_card_presences`. Provide an empty value to unset this control.
