---@class stripe.CreateSourceRequest
---@field amount? number Amount associated with the source. This is the amount for which the source will be chargeable once ready. Required for `single_use` sources. Not supported for `receiver` type sources, where charge amount may not be specified until funds land.
---@field currency? string Three-letter [ISO code for the currency](https://stripe.com/docs/currencies) associated with the source. This is the currency for which the source will be chargeable once ready.
---@field customer? string The `Customer` to whom the original source is attached to. Must be set when the original source is not a `Source` (e.g., `Card`).
---@field expand? stripe.CreateSourceRequestExpandList Specifies which fields in the response should be expanded.
---@field flow? stripe.CreateSourceRequestFlow|string The authentication `flow` of the source to create. `flow` is one of `redirect`, `receiver`, `code_verification`, `none`. It is generally inferred unless a type supports multiple flows.
---@field mandate? stripe.CreateSourceRequestMandate Information about a mandate possibility attached to a source object (generally for bank debits) as well as its acceptance status.
---@field metadata? stripe.CreateSourceRequestMetadataMap
---@field original_source? string The source to share.
---@field owner? stripe.CreateSourceRequestOwner Information about the owner of the payment instrument that may be used or required by particular source types.
---@field receiver? stripe.CreateSourceRequestReceiver Optional parameters for the receiver flow. Can be set only if the source is a receiver (`flow` is `receiver`).
---@field redirect? stripe.CreateSourceRequestRedirect Parameters required for the redirect flow. Required if the source is authenticated by a redirect (`flow` is `redirect`).
---@field source_order? stripe.CreateSourceRequestSourceOrder Information about the items and shipping associated with the source. Required for transactional credit (for example Klarna) sources before you can charge it.
---@field statement_descriptor? string An arbitrary string to be displayed on your customer's statement. As an example, if your website is `RunClub` and the item you're charging for is a race ticket, you may want to specify a `statement_descriptor` of `RunClub 5K race ticket.` While many payment types will display this information, some may not display it at all.
---@field token? string An optional token used to create the source. When passed, token properties will override source parameters.
---@field type? string The `type` of the source to create. Required unless `customer` and `original_source` are specified (see the [Cloning card Sources](https://docs.stripe.com/sources/connect#cloning-card-sources) guide)
---@field usage? stripe.CreateSourceRequestUsage|string
---@field idempotencyKey? string A unique key (up to 255 characters, for example a V4 UUID) that makes a retry of this request safe: Stripe returns the first result for a repeated key instead of performing the operation twice. See https://docs.stripe.com/api/idempotent_requests.

---Specifies which fields in the response should be expanded.
---@alias stripe.CreateSourceRequestExpandList string[]

---The authentication `flow` of the source to create. `flow` is one of `redirect`, `receiver`, `code_verification`, `none`. It is generally inferred unless a type supports multiple flows.
