---@class stripe.CreateSubscriptionRequest
---@field add_invoice_items? stripe.CreateSubscriptionRequestAddInvoiceItemsList A list of prices and quantities that will generate invoice items appended to the next invoice for this subscription. You may pass up to 20 items.
---@field application_fee_percent? stripe.CreateSubscriptionRequestApplicationFeePercent A non-negative decimal between 0 and 100, with at most two decimal places. This represents the percentage of the subscription invoice total that will be transferred to the application owner's Stripe account. The request must be made by a platform account on a connected account in order to set an application fee percentage. For more information, see the application fees [documentation](https://stripe.com/docs/connect/subscriptions#collecting-fees-on-subscriptions).
---@field automatic_tax? stripe.CreateSubscriptionRequestAutomaticTax Automatic tax settings for this subscription.
---@field backdate_start_date? number A past timestamp to backdate the subscription's start date to. If set, the first invoice will contain line items for the timespan between the start date and the current time. Can be combined with trials and the billing cycle anchor.
---@field billing_cycle_anchor? number A future timestamp in UTC format to anchor the subscription's [billing cycle](https://docs.stripe.com/subscriptions/billing-cycle). The anchor is the reference point that aligns future billing cycle dates. It sets the day of week for `week` intervals, the day of month for `month` and `year` intervals, and the month of year for `year` intervals.
---@field billing_cycle_anchor_config? stripe.CreateSubscriptionRequestBillingCycleAnchorConfig Mutually exclusive with billing_cycle_anchor and only valid with monthly and yearly price intervals. When provided, the billing_cycle_anchor is set to the next occurrence of the day_of_month at the hour, minute, and second UTC.
---@field billing_mode? stripe.CreateSubscriptionRequestBillingMode Controls how prorations and invoices for subscriptions are calculated and orchestrated.
---@field billing_schedules? stripe.CreateSubscriptionRequestBillingSchedulesList An array of billing schedules, which allow you to bill customers in advance for multiple service periods. Requires flexible billing mode and API version 2026-05-27.dahlia or later. Learn more about [prebilling](https://docs.stripe.com/billing/subscriptions/prebilling).
---@field billing_thresholds? stripe.CreateSubscriptionRequestBillingThresholds Define thresholds at which an invoice will be sent, and the subscription advanced to a new billing period. When updating, pass an empty string to remove previously-defined thresholds.
---@field cancel_at? stripe.CreateSubscriptionRequestCancelAt A timestamp at which the subscription should cancel. If set to a date before the current period ends, this will cause a proration if prorations have been enabled using `proration_behavior`. If set during a future period, this will always cause a proration for that period.
---@field cancel_at_period_end? boolean Indicate whether this subscription should cancel at the end of the current period (`current_period_end`). Defaults to `false`.
---@field collection_method? stripe.CreateSubscriptionRequestCollectionMethod|string Either `charge_automatically`, or `send_invoice`. When charging automatically, Stripe will attempt to pay this subscription at the end of the cycle using the default source attached to the customer. When sending an invoice, Stripe will email your customer an invoice with payment instructions and mark the subscription as `active`. Defaults to `charge_automatically`.
---@field currency? string Three-letter [ISO currency code](https://www.iso.org/iso-4217-currency-codes.html), in lowercase. Must be a [supported currency](https://stripe.com/docs/currencies).
---@field customer? string The identifier of the customer to subscribe.
---@field customer_account? string The identifier of the account representing the customer to subscribe.
---@field days_until_due? number Number of days a customer has to pay invoices generated by this subscription. Valid only for subscriptions where `collection_method` is set to `send_invoice`.
---@field default_payment_method? string ID of the default payment method for the subscription. It must belong to the customer associated with the subscription. This takes precedence over `default_source`. If neither are set, invoices will use the customer's [invoice_settings.default_payment_method](https://docs.stripe.com/api/customers/object#customer_object-invoice_settings-default_payment_method) or [default_source](https://docs.stripe.com/api/customers/object#customer_object-default_source).
---@field default_source? string ID of the default payment source for the subscription. It must belong to the customer associated with the subscription and be in a chargeable state. If `default_payment_method` is also set, `default_payment_method` will take precedence. If neither are set, invoices will use the customer's [invoice_settings.default_payment_method](https://docs.stripe.com/api/customers/object#customer_object-invoice_settings-default_payment_method) or [default_source](https://docs.stripe.com/api/customers/object#customer_object-default_source).
---@field default_tax_rates? stripe.CreateSubscriptionRequestDefaultTaxRates The tax rates that will apply to any subscription item that does not have `tax_rates` set. Invoices created will have their `default_tax_rates` populated from the subscription.
---@field description? string The subscription's description, meant to be displayable to the customer. Use this field to optionally store an explanation of the subscription for rendering in Stripe surfaces and certain local payment methods UIs.
---@field discounts? stripe.CreateSubscriptionRequestDiscounts The coupons to redeem into discounts for the subscription. If not specified or empty, inherits the discount from the subscription's customer.
---@field expand? stripe.CreateSubscriptionRequestExpandList Specifies which fields in the response should be expanded.
---@field invoice_settings? stripe.CreateSubscriptionRequestInvoiceSettings All invoices will be billed using the specified settings.
---@field items? stripe.CreateSubscriptionRequestItemsList A list of up to 20 subscription items, each with an attached price.
---@field metadata? stripe.CreateSubscriptionRequestMetadata Set of [key-value pairs](https://docs.stripe.com/api/metadata) that you can attach to an object. This can be useful for storing additional information about the object in a structured format. Individual keys can be unset by posting an empty value to them. All keys can be unset by posting an empty value to `metadata`.
---@field off_session? boolean Indicates if a customer is on or off-session while an invoice payment is attempted. Defaults to `false` (on-session).
---@field on_behalf_of? stripe.CreateSubscriptionRequestOnBehalfOf The account on behalf of which to charge, for each of the subscription's invoices.
---@field payment_behavior? stripe.CreateSubscriptionRequestPaymentBehavior|string Controls how Stripe handles the first invoice when payment is required and `collection_method=charge_automatically`. Subscriptions with `collection_method=send_invoice` are automatically activated regardless of the first Invoice status.
---@field payment_settings? stripe.CreateSubscriptionRequestPaymentSettings Payment settings to pass to invoices created by the subscription.
---@field pending_invoice_item_interval? stripe.CreateSubscriptionRequestPendingInvoiceItemInterval Specifies an interval for how often to bill for any pending invoice items. It is analogous to calling [Create an invoice](/api/invoices/create) for the given subscription at the specified interval.
---@field proration_behavior? stripe.CreateSubscriptionRequestProrationBehavior|string Determines how to handle [prorations](https://docs.stripe.com/billing/subscriptions/prorations) resulting from the `billing_cycle_anchor`. If no value is passed, the default is `create_prorations`.
---@field transfer_data? stripe.CreateSubscriptionRequestTransferData If specified, the funds from the subscription's invoices will be transferred to the destination and the ID of the resulting transfers will be found on the resulting charges.
---@field trial_end? stripe.CreateSubscriptionRequestTrialEnd Unix timestamp representing the end of the trial period the customer will get before being charged for the first time. If set, trial_end will override the default trial period of the plan the customer is being subscribed to. The special value `now` can be provided to end the customer's trial immediately. Can be at most two years from `billing_cycle_anchor`. See [Using trial periods on subscriptions](https://docs.stripe.com/billing/subscriptions/trials/free-trials) to learn more.
---@field trial_from_plan? boolean Indicates if a plan's `trial_period_days` should be applied to the subscription. Setting `trial_end` per subscription is preferred, and this defaults to `false`. Setting this flag to `true` together with `trial_end` is not allowed. See [Using trial periods on subscriptions](https://docs.stripe.com/billing/subscriptions/trials/free-trials) to learn more.
---@field trial_period_days? number Integer representing the number of trial period days before the customer is charged for the first time. This will always overwrite any trials that might apply via a subscribed plan. See [Using trial periods on subscriptions](https://docs.stripe.com/billing/subscriptions/trials/free-trials) to learn more.
---@field trial_settings? stripe.CreateSubscriptionRequestTrialSettings Settings related to subscription trials.
---@field idempotencyKey? string A unique key (up to 255 characters, for example a V4 UUID) that makes a retry of this request safe: Stripe returns the first result for a repeated key instead of performing the operation twice. See https://docs.stripe.com/api/idempotent_requests.

