---@class stripe.CreateTaxCalculationRequestLineItemsItem
---@field amount number A positive integer representing the line item's total price in the [smallest currency unit](https://docs.stripe.com/currencies#minor-units). If `tax_behavior=inclusive`, then this amount includes taxes. Otherwise, taxes are calculated on top of this amount.
---@field metadata? stripe.CreateTaxCalculationRequestLineItemsItemMetadataMap Set of [key-value pairs](https://docs.stripe.com/api/metadata) that you can attach to an object. This can be useful for storing additional information about the object in a structured format.
---@field performance_location? string A tax location ID. Depending on the [tax code](/tax/tax-for-tickets/reference/tax-location-performance), this is required, optional, or not supported.
---@field product? string If provided, the product's `tax_code` will be used as the line item's `tax_code`.
---@field quantity? number The number of units of the item being purchased. Used to calculate the per-unit price from the total `amount` for the line. For example, if `amount=100` and `quantity=4`, the calculated unit price is 25.
---@field reference? string A custom identifier for this line item, which must be unique across the line items in the calculation. The reference helps identify each line item in exported [tax reports](https://docs.stripe.com/tax/reports).
---@field tax_behavior? stripe.CreateTaxCalculationRequestLineItemsItemTaxBehavior|string Specifies whether the `amount` includes taxes. Defaults to `exclusive`.
---@field tax_code? string A [tax code](https://docs.stripe.com/tax/tax-categories) ID to use for this line item. If not provided, we will use the tax code from the provided `product` param. If neither `tax_code` nor `product` is provided, we will use the default tax code from your Tax Settings.

---Set of [key-value pairs](https://docs.stripe.com/api/metadata) that you can attach to an object. This can be useful for storing additional information about the object in a structured format.
---@alias stripe.CreateTaxCalculationRequestLineItemsItemMetadataMap { [string]: string }

---Specifies whether the `amount` includes taxes. Defaults to `exclusive`.
---@alias stripe.CreateTaxCalculationRequestLineItemsItemTaxBehavior "exclusive"|"inclusive"

---A list of items the customer is purchasing. You can pass up to 100 line items, or 1,000 if your account has an increased limit.
---@alias stripe.CreateTaxCalculationRequestLineItemsList stripe.CreateTaxCalculationRequestLineItemsItem[]

