---@class stripe.CreateTerminalConnectionTokenRequest
---@field expand? stripe.CreateTerminalConnectionTokenRequestExpandList Specifies which fields in the response should be expanded.
---@field location? string The id of the location that this connection token is scoped to. If specified the connection token will only be usable with readers assigned to that location, otherwise the connection token will be usable with all readers. Note that location scoping only applies to internet-connected readers. For more details, see [the docs on scoping connection tokens](https://docs.stripe.com/terminal/fleet/locations-and-zones?dashboard-or-api=api#connection-tokens).
---@field idempotencyKey? string A unique key (up to 255 characters, for example a V4 UUID) that makes a retry of this request safe: Stripe returns the first result for a repeated key instead of performing the operation twice. See https://docs.stripe.com/api/idempotent_requests.

---Specifies which fields in the response should be expanded.
---@alias stripe.CreateTerminalConnectionTokenRequestExpandList string[]

