---@class stripe.CreateTestHelpersIssuingAuthorizationRequest
---@field amount? number The total amount to attempt to authorize. This amount is in the provided currency, or defaults to the card's currency, and in the [smallest currency unit](https://docs.stripe.com/currencies#zero-decimal).
---@field amount_details? stripe.CreateTestHelpersIssuingAuthorizationRequestAmountDetails Detailed breakdown of amount components. These amounts are denominated in `currency` and in the [smallest currency unit](https://docs.stripe.com/currencies#zero-decimal).
---@field authorization_method? stripe.CreateTestHelpersIssuingAuthorizationRequestAuthorizationMethod|string How the card details were provided. Defaults to online.
---@field card string Card associated with this authorization.
---@field currency? string The currency of the authorization. If not provided, defaults to the currency of the card. Three-letter [ISO currency code](https://www.iso.org/iso-4217-currency-codes.html), in lowercase. Must be a [supported currency](https://stripe.com/docs/currencies).
---@field expand? stripe.CreateTestHelpersIssuingAuthorizationRequestExpandList Specifies which fields in the response should be expanded.
---@field fleet? stripe.CreateTestHelpersIssuingAuthorizationRequestFleet Fleet-specific information for authorizations using Fleet cards.
---@field fraud_disputability_likelihood? stripe.CreateTestHelpersIssuingAuthorizationRequestFraudDisputabilityLikelihood|string Probability that this transaction can be disputed in the event of fraud. Assessed by comparing the characteristics of the authorization to card network rules.
---@field fuel? stripe.CreateTestHelpersIssuingAuthorizationRequestFuel Information about fuel that was purchased with this transaction.
---@field is_amount_controllable? boolean If set `true`, you may provide [amount](https://docs.stripe.com/api/issuing/authorizations/approve#approve_issuing_authorization-amount) to control how much to hold for the authorization.
---@field merchant_amount? number The total amount to attempt to authorize. This amount is in the provided merchant currency, and in the [smallest currency unit](https://docs.stripe.com/currencies#zero-decimal).
---@field merchant_currency? string The currency of the authorization. If not provided, defaults to the currency of the card. Three-letter [ISO currency code](https://www.iso.org/iso-4217-currency-codes.html), in lowercase. Must be a [supported currency](https://stripe.com/docs/currencies).
---@field merchant_data? stripe.CreateTestHelpersIssuingAuthorizationRequestMerchantData Details about the seller (grocery store, e-commerce website, etc.) where the card authorization happened.
---@field network_data? stripe.CreateTestHelpersIssuingAuthorizationRequestNetworkData Details about the authorization, such as identifiers, set by the card network.
---@field risk_assessment? stripe.CreateTestHelpersIssuingAuthorizationRequestRiskAssessment Stripe’s assessment of the fraud risk for this authorization.
---@field verification_data? stripe.CreateTestHelpersIssuingAuthorizationRequestVerificationData Verifications that Stripe performed on information that the cardholder provided to the merchant.
---@field wallet? stripe.CreateTestHelpersIssuingAuthorizationRequestWallet|string The digital wallet used for this transaction. One of `apple_pay`, `google_pay`, or `samsung_pay`. Will populate as `null` when no digital wallet was utilized.
---@field idempotencyKey? string A unique key (up to 255 characters, for example a V4 UUID) that makes a retry of this request safe: Stripe returns the first result for a repeated key instead of performing the operation twice. See https://docs.stripe.com/api/idempotent_requests.

---Detailed breakdown of amount components. These amounts are denominated in `currency` and in the [smallest currency unit](https://docs.stripe.com/currencies#zero-decimal).
