---The reason why the card was canceled.
---@alias stripe.IssuingCardCancellationReason "design_rejected"|"fulfillment_error"|"lost"|"stolen"

---@class stripe.IssuingCardFraudWarning
---@field started_at number|distilled.Null Timestamp of the most recent fraud warning.
---@field type stripe.IssuingCardFraudWarningType|distilled.Null The type of fraud warning that most recently took place on this card. This field updates with every new fraud warning, so the value changes over time. If populated, cancel and reissue the card.

---The type of fraud warning that most recently took place on this card. This field updates with every new fraud warning, so the value changes over time. If populated, cancel and reissue the card.
---@alias stripe.IssuingCardFraudWarningType "card_testing_exposure"|"fraud_dispute_filed"|"third_party_reported"|"user_indicated_fraud"

---@class stripe.IssuingCardGooglePay
---@field eligible boolean Google Pay Eligibility
---@field ineligible_reason stripe.IssuingCardGooglePayIneligibleReason|distilled.Null Reason the card is ineligible for Google Pay

---Reason the card is ineligible for Google Pay
---@alias stripe.IssuingCardGooglePayIneligibleReason "missing_agreement"|"missing_cardholder_contact"|"unsupported_region"

---@class stripe.IssuingCardLifecycleConditions
---@field payment_count number The card is automatically cancelled when it makes this number of non-zero payment authorizations and transactions. The count includes penny authorizations, but doesn't include non-payment actions, such as authorization advice.

---@class stripe.IssuingCardLifecycleControls
---@field cancel_after stripe.IssuingCardLifecycleConditions

---Set of [key-value pairs](https://docs.stripe.com/api/metadata) that you can attach to an object. This can be useful for storing additional information about the object in a structured format.
---@alias stripe.IssuingCardMetadataMap { [string]: string }

---String representing the object's type. Objects of the same type share the same value.
---@alias stripe.IssuingCardObject "issuing.card"

---The personalization design object belonging to this card.
---@alias stripe.IssuingCardPersonalizationDesign string|stripe.IssuingPersonalizationDesign

---The latest card that replaces this card, if any.
---@alias stripe.IssuingCardReplacedBy string|stripe.IssuingCard

---The card this card replaces, if any.
---@alias stripe.IssuingCardReplacementFor string|stripe.IssuingCard

---The reason why the previous card needed to be replaced.
---@alias stripe.IssuingCardReplacementReason "damaged"|"expired"|"fulfillment_error"|"lost"|"stolen"

---@class stripe.IssuingCardShipping
---@field address stripe.Address
---@field address_validation stripe.IssuingCardShippingAddressValidation|distilled.Null Address validation details for the shipment.
---@field business_name string|distilled.Null The name of the business at the shipping address, used on the shipping label to ensure delivery when the card is shipped to a cardholder's workplace.
---@field carrier stripe.IssuingCardShippingCarrier|distilled.Null The delivery company that shipped a card.
---@field customs stripe.IssuingCardShippingCustoms|distilled.Null Additional information that may be required for clearing customs.
---@field delivered_at? number|distilled.Null The time the card was reported as delivered. Null for undelivered or untracked shipments, or if Stripe has not recorded a delivery time.
---@field eta number|distilled.Null A unix timestamp representing a best estimate of when the card will be delivered.
---@field name string Recipient name.
---@field phone_number string|distilled.Null The phone number of the receiver of the shipment. Our courier partners will use this number to contact you in the event of card delivery issues. For individual shipments to the EU/UK, if this field is empty, we will provide them with the phone number provided when the cardholder was initially created.
---@field require_signature boolean|distilled.Null Whether a signature is required for card delivery. This feature is only supported for US users. Standard shipping service does not support signature on delivery. The default value for standard shipping service is false and for express and priority services is true.
---@field service stripe.IssuingCardShippingService Shipment service, such as `standard` or `express`.
---@field shipped_at? number|distilled.Null The time the card was reported as shipped. Null if Stripe has not recorded a shipment time.
---@field status stripe.IssuingCardShippingStatus|distilled.Null The delivery status of the card.
---@field tracking_number string|distilled.Null A tracking number for a card shipment.
---@field tracking_url string|distilled.Null A link to the shipping carrier's site where you can view detailed information about a card shipment.
---@field type stripe.IssuingCardShippingType Packaging options.

---@class stripe.IssuingCardShippingAddressValidation
---@field mode stripe.IssuingCardShippingAddressValidationMode The address validation capabilities to use.
---@field normalized_address stripe.Address|distilled.Null The normalized shipping address.
---@field result stripe.IssuingCardShippingAddressValidationResult|distilled.Null The validation result for the shipping address.

---The address validation capabilities to use.
---@alias stripe.IssuingCardShippingAddressValidationMode "disabled"|"normalization_only"|"validation_and_normalization"

---The validation result for the shipping address.
---@alias stripe.IssuingCardShippingAddressValidationResult "indeterminate"|"likely_deliverable"|"likely_undeliverable"

---The delivery company that shipped a card.
---@alias stripe.IssuingCardShippingCarrier "correos"|"dhl"|"fedex"|"royal_mail"|"usps"

---@class stripe.IssuingCardShippingCustoms
---@field eori_number string|distilled.Null A registration number used for customs in Europe. See [https://www.gov.uk/eori](https://www.gov.uk/eori) for the UK and [https://ec.europa.eu/taxation_customs/business/customs-procedures-import-and-export/customs-procedures/economic-operators-registration-and-identification-number-eori_en](https://ec.europa.eu/taxation_customs/business/customs-procedures-import-and-export/customs-procedures/economic-operators-registration-and-identification-number-eori_en) for the EU.

---Shipment service, such as `standard` or `express`.
---@alias stripe.IssuingCardShippingService "express"|"priority"|"standard"

---The delivery status of the card.
---@alias stripe.IssuingCardShippingStatus "canceled"|"delivered"|"failure"|"pending"|"returned"|"shipped"|"submitted"

---Packaging options.
---@alias stripe.IssuingCardShippingType "bulk"|"individual"

---@class stripe.IssuingCardSpendingLimit
---@field amount number Maximum amount allowed to spend per interval. This amount is in the card's currency and in the [smallest currency unit](https://docs.stripe.com/currencies#zero-decimal).
---@field categories stripe.IssuingCardSpendingLimitCategoriesList|distilled.Null Array of strings containing [categories](https://docs.stripe.com/api#issuing_authorization_object-merchant_data-category) this limit applies to. Omitting this field will apply the limit to all categories.
---@field interval stripe.IssuingCardSpendingLimitInterval Interval (or event) to which the amount applies.

