---@field google_pay stripe.IssuingCardGooglePay
---@field primary_account_identifier string|distilled.Null Unique identifier for a card used with digital wallets

---An Issuing `Cardholder` object represents an individual or business entity who is [issued](https://docs.stripe.com/issuing) cards.
---
---Related guide: [How to create a cardholder](https://docs.stripe.com/issuing/cards/virtual/issue-cards#create-cardholder)
---@class stripe.IssuingCardholder
---@field billing stripe.IssuingCardholderAddress
---@field company stripe.IssuingCardholderCompany|distilled.Null Additional information about a `company` cardholder.
---@field created number Time at which the object was created. Measured in seconds since the Unix epoch.
---@field email string|distilled.Null The cardholder's email address.
---@field id string Unique identifier for the object.
---@field individual stripe.IssuingCardholderIndividual|distilled.Null Additional information about an `individual` cardholder.
---@field livemode boolean If the object exists in live mode, the value is `true`. If the object exists in test mode, the value is `false`.
---@field metadata stripe.IssuingCardholderMetadataMap Set of [key-value pairs](https://docs.stripe.com/api/metadata) that you can attach to an object. This can be useful for storing additional information about the object in a structured format.
---@field name string The cardholder's name. This will be printed on cards issued to them.
---@field object stripe.IssuingCardholderObject String representing the object's type. Objects of the same type share the same value.
---@field phone_number string|distilled.Null The cardholder's phone number. This is required for all cardholders who will be creating EU cards. See the [3D Secure documentation](https://docs.stripe.com/issuing/3d-secure#when-is-3d-secure-applied) for more details.
---@field preferred_locales stripe.IssuingCardholderPreferredLocalesList|distilled.Null The cardholder’s preferred locales (languages), ordered by preference. Locales can be `de`, `en`, `es`, `fr`, or `it`. This changes the language of the [3D Secure flow](https://docs.stripe.com/issuing/3d-secure) and one-time password messages sent to the cardholder.
---@field requirements stripe.IssuingCardholderRequirements
---@field spending_controls stripe.IssuingCardholderAuthorizationControls|distilled.Null Rules that control spending across this cardholder's cards. Refer to our [documentation](https://docs.stripe.com/issuing/controls/spending-controls) for more details.
---@field status stripe.IssuingCardholderStatus Specifies whether to permit authorizations on this cardholder's cards.
---@field type stripe.IssuingCardholderType One of `individual` or `company`. See [Choose a cardholder type](https://docs.stripe.com/issuing/other/choose-cardholder) for more details.

---@class stripe.IssuingCardholderAddress
---@field address stripe.Address

---@class stripe.IssuingCardholderAuthorizationControls
---@field allowed_card_presences stripe.IssuingCardholderAuthorizationControlsAllowedCardPresencesList|distilled.Null Array of card presence statuses from which authorizations will be allowed. Possible options are `present`, `not_present`. All other statuses will be blocked. Cannot be set with `blocked_card_presences`. Provide an empty value to unset this control.
---@field allowed_categories stripe.IssuingCardholderAuthorizationControlsAllowedCategoriesList|distilled.Null Array of strings containing [categories](https://docs.stripe.com/api#issuing_authorization_object-merchant_data-category) of authorizations to allow. All other categories will be blocked. Cannot be set with `blocked_categories`.
---@field allowed_merchant_countries stripe.IssuingCardholderAuthorizationControlsAllowedMerchantCountriesList|distilled.Null Array of strings containing representing countries from which authorizations will be allowed. Authorizations from merchants in all other countries will be declined. Country codes should be ISO 3166 alpha-2 country codes (e.g. `US`). Cannot be set with `blocked_merchant_countries`. Provide an empty value to unset this control.
---@field blocked_card_presences stripe.IssuingCardholderAuthorizationControlsBlockedCardPresencesList|distilled.Null Array of card presence statuses from which authorizations will be declined. Possible options are `present`, `not_present`. Cannot be set with `allowed_card_presences`. Provide an empty value to unset this control.
---@field blocked_categories stripe.IssuingCardholderAuthorizationControlsBlockedCategoriesList|distilled.Null Array of strings containing [categories](https://docs.stripe.com/api#issuing_authorization_object-merchant_data-category) of authorizations to decline. All other categories will be allowed. Cannot be set with `allowed_categories`.
---@field blocked_merchant_countries stripe.IssuingCardholderAuthorizationControlsBlockedMerchantCountriesList|distilled.Null Array of strings containing representing countries from which authorizations will be declined. Country codes should be ISO 3166 alpha-2 country codes (e.g. `US`). Cannot be set with `allowed_merchant_countries`. Provide an empty value to unset this control.
---@field spending_limits stripe.IssuingCardholderAuthorizationControlsSpendingLimitsList|distilled.Null Limit spending with amount-based rules that apply across this cardholder's cards.
---@field spending_limits_currency string|distilled.Null Currency of the amounts within `spending_limits`.

---@alias stripe.IssuingCardholderAuthorizationControlsAllowedCardPresencesItem "not_present"|"present"

---Array of card presence statuses from which authorizations will be allowed. Possible options are `present`, `not_present`. All other statuses will be blocked. Cannot be set with `blocked_card_presences`. Provide an empty value to unset this control.
---@alias stripe.IssuingCardholderAuthorizationControlsAllowedCardPresencesList stripe.IssuingCardholderAuthorizationControlsAllowedCardPresencesItem[]

