---A payment link is a shareable URL that will take your customers to a hosted payment page. A payment link can be shared and used multiple times.
---
---When a customer opens a payment link it will open a new [checkout session](https://docs.stripe.com/api/checkout/sessions) to render the payment page. You can use [checkout session events](https://docs.stripe.com/api/events/types#event_types-checkout.session.completed) to track payments through payment links.
---
---Related guide: [Payment Links API](https://docs.stripe.com/payment-links)
---@class stripe.PaymentLink
---@field active boolean Whether the payment link's `url` is active. If `false`, customers visiting the URL will be shown a page saying that the link has been deactivated.
---@field after_completion stripe.PaymentLinksResourceAfterCompletion
---@field allow_promotion_codes boolean Whether user redeemable promotion codes are enabled.
---@field application stripe.PaymentLinkApplication|distilled.Null The ID of the Connect application that created the Payment Link.
---@field application_fee_amount number|distilled.Null The amount of the application fee (if any) that will be requested to be applied to the payment and transferred to the application owner's Stripe account.
---@field application_fee_percent number|distilled.Null This represents the percentage of the subscription invoice total that will be transferred to the application owner's Stripe account.
---@field automatic_tax stripe.PaymentLinksResourceAutomaticTax
---@field billing_address_collection stripe.PaymentLinkBillingAddressCollection Configuration for collecting the customer's billing address. Defaults to `auto`.
---@field consent_collection stripe.PaymentLinksResourceConsentCollection|distilled.Null When set, provides configuration to gather active consent from customers.
---@field currency string Three-letter [ISO currency code](https://www.iso.org/iso-4217-currency-codes.html), in lowercase. Must be a [supported currency](https://stripe.com/docs/currencies).
---@field custom_fields stripe.PaymentLinkCustomFieldsList Collect additional information from your customer using custom fields. Up to 3 fields are supported. You can't set this parameter if `ui_mode` is `elements`.
---@field custom_text stripe.PaymentLinksResourceCustomText
---@field customer_creation stripe.PaymentLinkCustomerCreation Configuration for Customer creation during checkout.
---@field id string Unique identifier for the object.
---@field inactive_message string|distilled.Null The custom message to be displayed to a customer when a payment link is no longer active.
---@field invoice_creation stripe.PaymentLinksResourceInvoiceCreation|distilled.Null Configuration for creating invoice for payment mode payment links.
---@field line_items? stripe.PaymentLinkLineItems The line items representing what is being sold.
---@field livemode boolean If the object exists in live mode, the value is `true`. If the object exists in test mode, the value is `false`.
---@field managed_payments stripe.PaymentPagesCheckoutSessionManagedPayments|distilled.Null Settings for Managed Payments for this Payment Link and resulting [CheckoutSessions](/api/checkout/sessions/object), [PaymentIntents](/api/payment_intents/object), [Invoices](/api/invoices/object), and [Subscriptions](/api/subscriptions/object).
---@field metadata stripe.PaymentLinkMetadataMap Set of [key-value pairs](https://docs.stripe.com/api/metadata) that you can attach to an object. This can be useful for storing additional information about the object in a structured format.
---@field name_collection? stripe.PaymentLinksResourceNameCollection
---@field object stripe.PaymentLinkObject String representing the object's type. Objects of the same type share the same value.
---@field on_behalf_of stripe.PaymentLinkOnBehalfOf|distilled.Null The account on behalf of which to charge. See the [Connect documentation](https://support.stripe.com/questions/sending-invoices-on-behalf-of-connected-accounts) for details.
---@field optional_items? stripe.PaymentLinkOptionalItemsList|distilled.Null The optional items presented to the customer at checkout.
---@field payment_intent_data stripe.PaymentLinksResourcePaymentIntentData|distilled.Null Indicates the parameters to be passed to PaymentIntent creation during checkout.
---@field payment_method_collection stripe.PaymentLinkPaymentMethodCollection Configuration for collecting a payment method during checkout. Defaults to `always`.
---@field payment_method_options stripe.PaymentLinksResourcePaymentMethodOptions|distilled.Null Payment-method-specific configuration.
---@field payment_method_types stripe.PaymentLinkPaymentMethodTypesList|distilled.Null The list of payment method types that customers can use. When `null`, Stripe will dynamically show relevant payment methods you've enabled in your [payment method settings](https://dashboard.stripe.com/settings/payment_methods).
---@field phone_number_collection stripe.PaymentLinksResourcePhoneNumberCollection
---@field restrictions stripe.PaymentLinksResourceRestrictions|distilled.Null Settings that restrict the usage of a payment link.
---@field shipping_address_collection stripe.PaymentLinksResourceShippingAddressCollection|distilled.Null Configuration for collecting the customer's shipping address.
---@field shipping_options stripe.PaymentLinkShippingOptionsList The shipping rate options applied to the session.
---@field submit_type stripe.PaymentLinkSubmitType Indicates the type of transaction being performed which customizes relevant text on the page, such as the submit button.
---@field subscription_data stripe.PaymentLinksResourceSubscriptionData|distilled.Null When creating a subscription, the specified configuration data will be used. There must be at least one line item with a recurring price to use `subscription_data`.
---@field tax_id_collection stripe.PaymentLinksResourceTaxIdCollection
---@field transfer_data stripe.PaymentLinksResourceTransferData|distilled.Null The account (if any) the payments will be attributed to for tax reporting, and where funds from each payment will be transferred to.
---@field url string The public URL that can be shared with customers.

