---@class stripe.PaymentMethodCard
---@field brand string Card brand. Can be `amex`, `cartes_bancaires`, `diners`, `discover`, `eftpos_au`, `jcb`, `link`, `mastercard`, `unionpay`, `visa` or `unknown`.
---@field checks stripe.PaymentMethodCardChecks|distilled.Null Checks on Card address and CVC if provided.
---@field country string|distilled.Null Two-letter ISO code representing the country of the card. You could use this attribute to get a sense of the international breakdown of cards you've collected.
---@field description? string|distilled.Null A high-level description of the type of cards issued in this range. (For internal use only and not typically available in standard API requests.)
---@field display_brand string|distilled.Null The brand to use when displaying the card, this accounts for customer's brand choice on dual-branded cards. Can be `american_express`, `cartes_bancaires`, `diners_club`, `discover`, `eftpos_australia`, `interac`, `jcb`, `mastercard`, `union_pay`, `visa`, or `other` and may contain more values in the future.
---@field exp_month number Two-digit number representing the card's expiration month.
---@field exp_year number Four-digit number representing the card's expiration year.
---@field fingerprint? string|distilled.Null Uniquely identifies this particular card number. You can use this attribute to check whether two customers who’ve signed up with you are using the same card number, for example. For payment methods that tokenize card information (Apple Pay, Google Pay), the tokenized number might be provided instead of the underlying card number. *As of May 1, 2021, card fingerprint in India for Connect changed to allow two fingerprints for the same card---one for India and one for the rest of the world.*
---@field funding string Card funding type. Can be `credit`, `debit`, `prepaid`, or `unknown`.
---@field generated_from stripe.PaymentMethodCardGeneratedCard|distilled.Null Details of the original PaymentMethod that created this object.
---@field iin? string|distilled.Null Issuer identification number of the card. (For internal use only and not typically available in standard API requests.)
---@field issuer? string|distilled.Null The name of the card's issuing bank. (For internal use only and not typically available in standard API requests.)
---@field last4 string The last four digits of the card.
---@field networks stripe.Networks|distilled.Null Contains information about card networks that can be used to process the payment.
---@field regulated_status stripe.PaymentMethodCardRegulatedStatus|distilled.Null Status of a card based on the card issuer.
---@field three_d_secure_usage stripe.ThreeDSecureUsage|distilled.Null Contains details on how this Card may be used for 3D Secure authentication.
---@field wallet stripe.PaymentMethodCardWallet|distilled.Null If this Card is part of a card wallet, this contains the details of the card wallet.

---@class stripe.PaymentMethodCardChecks
