---@class stripe.PaymentMethodInteracPresent
---@field brand string|distilled.Null Card brand. Can be `interac`, `mastercard` or `visa`.
---@field cardholder_name string|distilled.Null The cardholder name as read from the card, in [ISO 7813](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISO/IEC_7813) format. May include alphanumeric characters, special characters and first/last name separator (`/`). In some cases, the cardholder name may not be available depending on how the issuer has configured the card. Cardholder name is typically not available on swipe or contactless payments, such as those made with Apple Pay and Google Pay.
---@field country string|distilled.Null Two-letter ISO code representing the country of the card. You could use this attribute to get a sense of the international breakdown of cards you've collected.
---@field description? string|distilled.Null A high-level description of the type of cards issued in this range. (For internal use only and not typically available in standard API requests.)
---@field exp_month number Two-digit number representing the card's expiration month.
---@field exp_year number Four-digit number representing the card's expiration year.
---@field fingerprint string|distilled.Null Uniquely identifies this particular card number. You can use this attribute to check whether two customers who’ve signed up with you are using the same card number, for example. For payment methods that tokenize card information (Apple Pay, Google Pay), the tokenized number might be provided instead of the underlying card number. *As of May 1, 2021, card fingerprint in India for Connect changed to allow two fingerprints for the same card---one for India and one for the rest of the world.*
---@field funding string|distilled.Null Card funding type. Can be `credit`, `debit`, `prepaid`, or `unknown`.
---@field iin? string|distilled.Null Issuer identification number of the card. (For internal use only and not typically available in standard API requests.)
---@field issuer? string|distilled.Null The name of the card's issuing bank. (For internal use only and not typically available in standard API requests.)
---@field last4 string|distilled.Null The last four digits of the card.
---@field networks stripe.PaymentMethodCardPresentNetworks|distilled.Null Contains information about card networks that can be used to process the payment.
---@field preferred_locales stripe.PaymentMethodInteracPresentPreferredLocalesList|distilled.Null The languages that the issuing bank recommends using for localizing any customer-facing text, as read from the card. Referenced from EMV tag 5F2D, data encoded on the card's chip.
---@field read_method stripe.PaymentMethodInteracPresentReadMethod|distilled.Null How card details were read in this transaction.

---The languages that the issuing bank recommends using for localizing any customer-facing text, as read from the card. Referenced from EMV tag 5F2D, data encoded on the card's chip.
---@alias stripe.PaymentMethodInteracPresentPreferredLocalesList string[]

---How card details were read in this transaction.
---@alias stripe.PaymentMethodInteracPresentReadMethod "contact_emv"|"contactless_emv"|"contactless_magstripe_mode"|"magnetic_stripe_fallback"|"magnetic_stripe_track2"

