---Refund objects allow you to refund a previously created charge that isn't
---refunded yet. Funds are refunded to the credit or debit card that's
---initially charged.
---
---Related guide: [Refunds](https://docs.stripe.com/refunds)
---@class stripe.Refund
---@field amount number Amount, in cents (or local equivalent).
---@field balance_transaction stripe.RefundBalanceTransaction|distilled.Null Balance transaction that describes the impact on your account balance.
---@field charge stripe.RefundCharge|distilled.Null ID of the charge that's refunded.
---@field created number Time at which the object was created. Measured in seconds since the Unix epoch.
---@field currency string Three-letter [ISO currency code](https://www.iso.org/iso-4217-currency-codes.html), in lowercase. Must be a [supported currency](https://stripe.com/docs/currencies).
---@field customer stripe.RefundCustomer|distilled.Null ID of the customer of this refund.
---@field customer_account string|distilled.Null ID of the account of this refund.
---@field description? string An arbitrary string attached to the object. You can use this for displaying to users (available on non-card refunds only).
---@field destination_details? stripe.RefundDestinationDetails
---@field failure_balance_transaction? stripe.RefundFailureBalanceTransaction After the refund fails, this balance transaction describes the adjustment made on your account balance that reverses the initial balance transaction.
---@field failure_reason? string Provides the reason for the refund failure. Possible values are: `lost_or_stolen_card`, `expired_or_canceled_card`, `charge_for_pending_refund_disputed`, `insufficient_funds`, `declined`, `merchant_request`, or `unknown`.
---@field id string Unique identifier for the object.
---@field instructions_email? string For payment methods without native refund support (for example, Konbini, PromptPay), provide an email address for the customer to receive refund instructions.
---@field metadata stripe.RefundMetadataMap|distilled.Null Set of [key-value pairs](https://docs.stripe.com/api/metadata) that you can attach to an object. This can be useful for storing additional information about the object in a structured format.
---@field next_action? stripe.RefundNextAction
---@field object stripe.RefundObject String representing the object's type. Objects of the same type share the same value.
---@field payment_intent stripe.RefundPaymentIntent|distilled.Null ID of the PaymentIntent that's refunded.
---@field payment_method stripe.RefundPaymentMethod|distilled.Null ID of the payment method associated with this refund.
---@field pending_reason? stripe.RefundPendingReason Provides the reason for why the refund is pending. Possible values are: `processing`, `insufficient_funds`, or `charge_pending`.
---@field presentment_details? stripe.PaymentFlowsPaymentIntentPresentmentDetails
---@field reason stripe.RefundReason|distilled.Null Reason for the refund, which is either user-provided (`duplicate`, `fraudulent`, or `requested_by_customer`) or generated by Stripe internally (`expired_uncaptured_charge`).
---@field receipt_number string|distilled.Null This is the transaction number that appears on email receipts sent for this refund.
---@field source_transfer_reversal stripe.RefundSourceTransferReversal|distilled.Null The transfer reversal that's associated with the refund. Only present if the charge came from another Stripe account.
---@field status string|distilled.Null Status of the refund. This can be `pending`, `requires_action`, `succeeded`, `failed`, or `canceled`. Learn more about [failed refunds](https://docs.stripe.com/refunds#failed-refunds).
---@field transfer_reversal stripe.RefundTransferReversal|distilled.Null This refers to the transfer reversal object if the accompanying transfer reverses. This is only applicable if the charge was created using the destination parameter.

