---@class stripe.SmorResourceManagedPayments
---@field enabled boolean Set to `true` to enable [Managed Payments](https://docs.stripe.com/payments/managed-payments), Stripe's merchant of record solution, for this session.

---`Source` objects allow you to accept a variety of payment methods. They
---represent a customer's payment instrument, and can be used with the Stripe API
---just like a `Card` object: once chargeable, they can be charged, or can be
---attached to customers.
---
---This API is deprecated. Use the [PaymentMethods API](https://docs.stripe.com/api/payment_methods) instead.
---
---Related guides: [Sources API](https://docs.stripe.com/sources) and [Sources & Customers](https://docs.stripe.com/sources/customers).
---@class stripe.Source
---@field ach_credit_transfer? stripe.SourceTypeAchCreditTransfer
---@field ach_debit? stripe.SourceTypeAchDebit
---@field acss_debit? stripe.SourceTypeAcssDebit
---@field alipay? stripe.SourceTypeAlipay
---@field allow_redisplay stripe.SourceAllowRedisplay|distilled.Null This field indicates whether this payment method can be shown again to its customer in a checkout flow. Stripe products such as Checkout and Elements use this field to determine whether a payment method can be shown as a saved payment method in a checkout flow. The field defaults to “unspecified”.
---@field amount number|distilled.Null A positive integer in the smallest currency unit (that is, 100 cents for $1.00, or 1 for ¥1, Japanese Yen being a zero-decimal currency) representing the total amount associated with the source. This is the amount for which the source will be chargeable once ready. Required for `single_use` sources.
---@field au_becs_debit? stripe.SourceTypeAuBecsDebit
---@field bancontact? stripe.SourceTypeBancontact
---@field card? stripe.SourceTypeCard
---@field card_present? stripe.SourceTypeCardPresent
---@field client_secret distilled.Secret The client secret of the source. Used for client-side retrieval using a publishable key.
---@field code_verification? stripe.SourceCodeVerificationFlow
---@field created number Time at which the object was created. Measured in seconds since the Unix epoch.
---@field currency string|distilled.Null Three-letter [ISO code for the currency](https://stripe.com/docs/currencies) associated with the source. This is the currency for which the source will be chargeable once ready. Required for `single_use` sources.
---@field customer? string The ID of the customer to which this source is attached. This will not be present when the source has not been attached to a customer.
---@field eps? stripe.SourceTypeEps
---@field flow string The authentication `flow` of the source. `flow` is one of `redirect`, `receiver`, `code_verification`, `none`.
---@field giropay? stripe.SourceTypeGiropay
---@field id string Unique identifier for the object.
---@field ideal? stripe.SourceTypeIdeal
---@field klarna? stripe.SourceTypeKlarna
---@field livemode boolean If the object exists in live mode, the value is `true`. If the object exists in test mode, the value is `false`.
---@field metadata stripe.SourceMetadataMap|distilled.Null Set of [key-value pairs](https://docs.stripe.com/api/metadata) that you can attach to an object. This can be useful for storing additional information about the object in a structured format.
---@field multibanco? stripe.SourceTypeMultibanco
---@field object stripe.SourceObject String representing the object's type. Objects of the same type share the same value.
---@field owner stripe.SourceOwner|distilled.Null Information about the owner of the payment instrument that may be used or required by particular source types.
---@field p24? stripe.SourceTypeP24
---@field receiver? stripe.SourceReceiverFlow
---@field redirect? stripe.SourceRedirectFlow
---@field sepa_credit_transfer? stripe.SourceTypeSepaCreditTransfer
---@field sepa_debit? stripe.SourceTypeSepaDebit
---@field sofort? stripe.SourceTypeSofort
---@field source_order? stripe.SourceOrder
---@field statement_descriptor string|distilled.Null Extra information about a source. This will appear on your customer's statement every time you charge the source.
---@field status string The status of the source, one of `canceled`, `chargeable`, `consumed`, `failed`, or `pending`. Only `chargeable` sources can be used to create a charge.
---@field three_d_secure? stripe.SourceTypeThreeDSecure
---@field type stripe.SourceType The `type` of the source. The `type` is a payment method, one of `ach_credit_transfer`, `ach_debit`, `alipay`, `bancontact`, `card`, `card_present`, `eps`, `giropay`, `ideal`, `multibanco`, `klarna`, `p24`, `sepa_debit`, `sofort`, `three_d_secure`, or `wechat`. An additional hash is included on the source with a name matching this value. It contains additional information specific to the [payment method](https://docs.stripe.com/sources) used.
---@field usage string|distilled.Null Either `reusable` or `single_use`. Whether this source should be reusable or not. Some source types may or may not be reusable by construction, while others may leave the option at creation. If an incompatible value is passed, an error will be returned.
---@field wechat? stripe.SourceTypeWechat

---This field indicates whether this payment method can be shown again to its customer in a checkout flow. Stripe products such as Checkout and Elements use this field to determine whether a payment method can be shown as a saved payment method in a checkout flow. The field defaults to “unspecified”.
---@alias stripe.SourceAllowRedisplay "always"|"limited"|"unspecified"

