---A Tax Calculation allows you to calculate the tax to collect from your customer.
---
---Related guide: [Calculate tax in your custom payment flow](https://docs.stripe.com/tax/custom)
---@class stripe.TaxCalculation
---@field amount_total number Total amount after taxes in the [smallest currency unit](https://docs.stripe.com/currencies#minor-units).
---@field currency string Three-letter [ISO currency code](https://www.iso.org/iso-4217-currency-codes.html), in lowercase. Must be a [supported currency](https://stripe.com/docs/currencies).
---@field customer string|distilled.Null The ID of an existing [Customer](https://docs.stripe.com/api/customers/object) used for the resource.
---@field customer_details stripe.TaxProductResourceCustomerDetails
---@field expires_at number|distilled.Null Timestamp of date at which the tax calculation will expire.
---@field id string|distilled.Null Unique identifier for the calculation.
---@field line_items? stripe.TaxCalculationLineItems|distilled.Null The list of items the customer is purchasing.
---@field livemode boolean If the object exists in live mode, the value is `true`. If the object exists in test mode, the value is `false`.
---@field object stripe.TaxCalculationObject String representing the object's type. Objects of the same type share the same value.
---@field ship_from_details stripe.TaxProductResourceShipFromDetails|distilled.Null The details of the ship from location, such as the address.
---@field shipping_cost stripe.TaxProductResourceTaxCalculationShippingCost|distilled.Null The shipping cost details for the calculation.
---@field tax_amount_exclusive number The amount of tax to be collected on top of the line item prices.
---@field tax_amount_inclusive number The amount of tax already included in the line item prices.
---@field tax_breakdown stripe.TaxCalculationTaxBreakdownList Breakdown of individual tax amounts that add up to the total.
---@field tax_date number The calculation uses the tax rules and rates that are in effect at this timestamp. You can use a date up to 31 days in the past or up to 31 days in the future. If you use a future date, Stripe doesn't guarantee that the expected tax rules and rate being used match the actual rules and rate that will be in effect on that date. We deploy tax changes before their effective date, but not within a fixed window.

---A Tax Calculation Line Item represents a single item in a tax calculation.
