---
---Use [InboundTransfers](https://docs.stripe.com/docs/treasury/moving-money/financial-accounts/into/inbound-transfers) to add funds to your [FinancialAccount](https://docs.stripe.com/api#financial_accounts) via a PaymentMethod that is owned by you. The funds will be transferred via an ACH debit.
---
---Related guide: [Moving money with Treasury using InboundTransfer objects](https://docs.stripe.com/docs/treasury/moving-money/financial-accounts/into/inbound-transfers)
---@class stripe.TreasuryInboundTransfer
---@field amount number Amount (in cents) transferred.
---@field cancelable boolean Returns `true` if the InboundTransfer is able to be canceled.
---@field created number Time at which the object was created. Measured in seconds since the Unix epoch.
---@field currency string Three-letter [ISO currency code](https://www.iso.org/iso-4217-currency-codes.html), in lowercase. Must be a [supported currency](https://stripe.com/docs/currencies).
---@field description string|distilled.Null An arbitrary string attached to the object. Often useful for displaying to users.
---@field failure_details stripe.TreasuryInboundTransfersResourceFailureDetails|distilled.Null Details about this InboundTransfer's failure. Will be set when `status=failed` or `returned=true`.
---@field financial_account string The FinancialAccount that received the funds.
---@field hosted_regulatory_receipt_url string|distilled.Null A [hosted transaction receipt](https://docs.stripe.com/treasury/moving-money/regulatory-receipts) URL that is provided when money movement is considered regulated under Stripe's money transmission licenses.
---@field id string Unique identifier for the object.
---@field linked_flows stripe.TreasuryInboundTransfersResourceInboundTransferResourceLinkedFlows
---@field livemode boolean If the object exists in live mode, the value is `true`. If the object exists in test mode, the value is `false`.
---@field metadata stripe.TreasuryInboundTransferMetadataMap Set of [key-value pairs](https://docs.stripe.com/api/metadata) that you can attach to an object. This can be useful for storing additional information about the object in a structured format.
---@field object stripe.TreasuryInboundTransferObject String representing the object's type. Objects of the same type share the same value.
---@field origin_payment_method string|distilled.Null The origin payment method to be debited for an InboundTransfer.
---@field origin_payment_method_details stripe.InboundTransfers|distilled.Null Details about the PaymentMethod for an InboundTransfer.
---@field returned boolean|distilled.Null Returns `true` if the funds for an InboundTransfer were returned after the InboundTransfer went to the `succeeded` state.
---@field statement_descriptor string Statement descriptor shown when funds are debited from the source. Not all payment networks support `statement_descriptor`.
---@field status stripe.TreasuryInboundTransferStatus Status of the InboundTransfer: `processing`, `succeeded`, `failed`, and `canceled`. An InboundTransfer is `processing` if it is created and pending. The status changes to `succeeded` once the funds have been "confirmed" and a `transaction` is created and posted. The status changes to `failed` if the transfer fails.
---@field status_transitions stripe.TreasuryInboundTransfersResourceInboundTransferResourceStatusTransitions
---@field transaction stripe.TreasuryInboundTransferTransaction|distilled.Null The Transaction associated with this object.

