---@class stripe.TreasuryOutboundPayment
---@field amount number Amount (in cents) transferred.
---@field cancelable boolean Returns `true` if the object can be canceled, and `false` otherwise.
---@field created number Time at which the object was created. Measured in seconds since the Unix epoch.
---@field currency string Three-letter [ISO currency code](https://www.iso.org/iso-4217-currency-codes.html), in lowercase. Must be a [supported currency](https://stripe.com/docs/currencies).
---@field customer string|distilled.Null ID of the [customer](https://docs.stripe.com/api/customers) to whom an OutboundPayment is sent.
---@field description string|distilled.Null An arbitrary string attached to the object. Often useful for displaying to users.
---@field destination_payment_method string|distilled.Null The PaymentMethod via which an OutboundPayment is sent. This field can be empty if the OutboundPayment was created using `destination_payment_method_data`.
---@field destination_payment_method_details stripe.OutboundPaymentsPaymentMethodDetails|distilled.Null Details about the PaymentMethod for an OutboundPayment.
---@field end_user_details stripe.TreasuryOutboundPaymentsResourceOutboundPaymentResourceEndUserDetails|distilled.Null Details about the end user.
---@field expected_arrival_date number The date when funds are expected to arrive in the destination account.
---@field financial_account string The FinancialAccount that funds were pulled from.
---@field hosted_regulatory_receipt_url string|distilled.Null A [hosted transaction receipt](https://docs.stripe.com/treasury/moving-money/regulatory-receipts) URL that is provided when money movement is considered regulated under Stripe's money transmission licenses.
---@field id string Unique identifier for the object.
---@field livemode boolean If the object exists in live mode, the value is `true`. If the object exists in test mode, the value is `false`.
---@field metadata stripe.TreasuryOutboundPaymentMetadataMap Set of [key-value pairs](https://docs.stripe.com/api/metadata) that you can attach to an object. This can be useful for storing additional information about the object in a structured format.
---@field object stripe.TreasuryOutboundPaymentObject String representing the object's type. Objects of the same type share the same value.
---@field returned_details stripe.TreasuryOutboundPaymentsResourceReturnedStatus|distilled.Null Details about a returned OutboundPayment. Only set when the status is `returned`.
---@field statement_descriptor string The description that appears on the receiving end for an OutboundPayment (for example, bank statement for external bank transfer).
---@field status stripe.TreasuryOutboundPaymentStatus Current status of the OutboundPayment: `processing`, `failed`, `posted`, `returned`, `canceled`. An OutboundPayment is `processing` if it has been created and is pending. The status changes to `posted` once the OutboundPayment has been "confirmed" and funds have left the account, or to `failed` or `canceled`. If an OutboundPayment fails to arrive at its destination, its status will change to `returned`.
