---Information about the company or business. This field is available for any `business_type`. Once you create an [Account Link](/api/account_links) or [Account Session](/api/account_sessions), this property can only be updated for accounts where [controller.requirement_collection](/api/accounts/object#account_object-controller-requirement_collection) is `application`, which includes Custom accounts.
---@class stripe.UpdateAccountRequestCompany
---@field address? stripe.UpdateAccountRequestCompanyAddress The company's primary address.
---@field address_kana? stripe.UpdateAccountRequestCompanyAddressKana The Kana variation of the company's primary address (Japan only).
---@field address_kanji? stripe.UpdateAccountRequestCompanyAddressKanji The Kanji variation of the company's primary address (Japan only).
---@field administrative_address? stripe.UpdateAccountRequestCompanyAdministrativeAddress The location where the business is administered.
---@field directors_provided? boolean Whether the company's directors have been provided. Set this Boolean to `true` after creating all the company's directors with [the Persons API](/api/persons) for accounts with a `relationship.director` requirement. This value is not automatically set to `true` after creating directors, so it needs to be updated to indicate all directors have been provided.
---@field directorship_declaration? stripe.UpdateAccountRequestCompanyDirectorshipDeclaration This hash is used to attest that the directors information provided to Stripe is both current and correct.
---@field executives_provided? boolean Whether the company's executives have been provided. Set this Boolean to `true` after creating all the company's executives with [the Persons API](/api/persons) for accounts with a `relationship.executive` requirement.
---@field export_license_id? string The export license ID number of the company, also referred as Import Export Code (India only).
---@field export_purpose_code? string The purpose code to use for export transactions (India only).
---@field name? string The company's legal name.
---@field name_kana? string The Kana variation of the company's legal name (Japan only).
---@field name_kanji? string The Kanji variation of the company's legal name (Japan only).
---@field owners_provided? boolean Whether the company's owners have been provided. Set this Boolean to `true` after creating all the company's owners with [the Persons API](/api/persons) for accounts with a `relationship.owner` requirement.
---@field ownership_declaration? stripe.UpdateAccountRequestCompanyOwnershipDeclaration This hash is used to attest that the beneficial owner information provided to Stripe is both current and correct.
---@field ownership_exemption_reason? stripe.UpdateAccountRequestCompanyOwnershipExemptionReason|string This value is used to determine if a business is exempt from providing ultimate beneficial owners. See [this support article](https://support.stripe.com/questions/exemption-from-providing-ownership-details) and [changelog](https://docs.stripe.com/changelog/acacia/2025-01-27/ownership-exemption-reason-accounts-api) for more details.
---@field phone? string The company's phone number (used for verification).
---@field physical_address? stripe.UpdateAccountRequestCompanyPhysicalAddress A location where the business has a meaningful physical operating presence.
---@field principal_place_of_business? stripe.UpdateAccountRequestCompanyPrincipalPlaceOfBusiness The primary location where the business conducts operations.
---@field registration_date? stripe.UpdateAccountRequestCompanyRegistrationDate
---@field registration_number? string The identification number given to a company when it is registered or incorporated, if distinct from the identification number used for filing taxes. (Examples are the CIN for companies and LLP IN for partnerships in India, and the Company Registration Number in Hong Kong).
---@field representative_declaration? stripe.UpdateAccountRequestCompanyRepresentativeDeclaration This hash is used to attest that the representative is authorized to act as the representative of their legal entity.
---@field structure? stripe.UpdateAccountRequestCompanyStructure|string The category identifying the legal structure of the company or legal entity. See [Business structure](/connect/identity-verification#business-structure) for more details. Pass an empty string to unset this value.
---@field tax_id? string The business ID number of the company, as appropriate for the company’s country. (Examples are an Employer ID Number in the U.S., a Business Number in Canada, or a Company Number in the UK.) Changing this value requires that the account re-accept the [terms of service](/api/accounts/object#account_object-tos_acceptance).
---@field tax_id_registrar? string The jurisdiction in which the `tax_id` is registered (Germany-based companies only).
---@field vat_id? string The VAT number of the company.
---@field verification? stripe.UpdateAccountRequestCompanyVerification Information on the verification state of the company.

---The company's primary address.
---@class stripe.UpdateAccountRequestCompanyAddress
---@field city? string City, district, suburb, town, or village.
---@field country? string Two-letter country code ([ISO 3166-1 alpha-2](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISO_3166-1_alpha-2)).
---@field line1? string Address line 1, such as the street, PO Box, or company name.
---@field line2? string Address line 2, such as the apartment, suite, unit, or building.
---@field postal_code? string ZIP or postal code.
---@field state? string State, county, province, or region ([ISO 3166-2](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISO_3166-2)).

---The Kana variation of the company's primary address (Japan only).
---@class stripe.UpdateAccountRequestCompanyAddressKana
---@field city? string City or ward.
---@field country? string Two-letter country code ([ISO 3166-1 alpha-2](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISO_3166-1_alpha-2)).
---@field line1? string Block or building number.
---@field line2? string Building details.
---@field postal_code? string Postal code.
---@field state? string Prefecture.
---@field town? string Town or cho-me.

---The Kanji variation of the company's primary address (Japan only).
