---@class stripe.UpdateCoreAccountRequest
---@field id string The ID of the Account to update.
---@field account_token? string The account token generated by the account token API.
---@field configuration? stripe.UpdateCoreAccountRequestConfiguration An Account Configuration which allows the Account to take on a key persona across Stripe products.
---@field contact_email? string The primary contact email address for the Account.
---@field contact_phone? string The default contact phone for the Account.
---@field dashboard? stripe.UpdateCoreAccountRequestDashboard|string A value indicating the Stripe dashboard this Account has access to. This will depend on which configurations are enabled for this account.
---@field defaults? stripe.UpdateCoreAccountRequestDefaults Default values to be used on Account Configurations.
---@field display_name? string A descriptive name for the Account. This name will be surfaced in the Stripe Dashboard and on any invoices sent to the Account.
---@field identity? stripe.UpdateCoreAccountRequestIdentity Information about the company, individual, and business represented by the Account.
---@field include? stripe.UpdateCoreAccountRequestIncludeList Additional fields to include in the response.
---@field metadata? stripe.UpdateCoreAccountRequestMetadataMap Set of key-value pairs that you can attach to an object. This can be useful for storing additional information about the object in a structured format.
---@field idempotencyKey? string A unique key (up to 255 characters, for example a V4 UUID) that makes a retry of this request safe: Stripe returns the first result for a repeated key instead of performing the operation twice. See https://docs.stripe.com/api/idempotent_requests.

---An Account Configuration which allows the Account to take on a key persona across Stripe products.
---@class stripe.UpdateCoreAccountRequestConfiguration
---@field customer? stripe.UpdateCoreAccountRequestConfigurationCustomer The Customer Configuration allows the Account to be charged.
---@field merchant? stripe.UpdateCoreAccountRequestConfigurationMerchant Enables the Account to act as a connected account and collect payments facilitated by a Connect platform. You must onboard your platform to Connect before you can add this configuration to your connected accounts. Utilize this configuration when the Account will be the Merchant of Record, like with Direct charges or Destination Charges with on_behalf_of set.
---@field recipient? stripe.UpdateCoreAccountRequestConfigurationRecipient The Recipient Configuration allows the Account to receive funds. Utilize this configuration if the Account will not be the Merchant of Record, like with Separate Charges & Transfers, or Destination Charges without on_behalf_of set.

---The Customer Configuration allows the Account to be charged.
