---@field applied? boolean Represents the state of the configuration, and can be updated to deactivate or re-apply a configuration.
---@field automatic_indirect_tax? stripe.UpdateCoreAccountRequestConfigurationCustomerAutomaticIndirectTax Automatic indirect tax settings to be used when automatic tax calculation is enabled on the customer's invoices, subscriptions, checkout sessions, or payment links. Surfaces if automatic tax calculation is possible given the current customer location information.
---@field billing? stripe.UpdateCoreAccountRequestConfigurationCustomerBilling Billing settings - default settings used for this customer in Billing flows such as Invoices and Subscriptions.
---@field capabilities? stripe.UpdateCoreAccountRequestConfigurationCustomerCapabilities Capabilities that have been requested on the Customer Configuration.
---@field shipping? stripe.UpdateCoreAccountRequestConfigurationCustomerShipping The customer's shipping information. Appears on invoices emailed to this customer.
---@field test_clock? string ID of the test clock to attach to the customer. Can only be set on testmode Accounts, and when the Customer Configuration is first set on an Account.

---Automatic indirect tax settings to be used when automatic tax calculation is enabled on the customer's invoices, subscriptions, checkout sessions, or payment links. Surfaces if automatic tax calculation is possible given the current customer location information.
---@class stripe.UpdateCoreAccountRequestConfigurationCustomerAutomaticIndirectTax
---@field exempt? stripe.UpdateCoreAccountRequestConfigurationCustomerAutomaticIndirectTaxExempt|string The customer account's tax exemption status: `none`, `exempt`, or `reverse`. When `reverse`, invoice and receipt PDFs include "Reverse charge".
---@field ip_address? string A recent IP address of the customer used for tax reporting and tax location inference.
---@field validate_location? stripe.UpdateCoreAccountRequestConfigurationCustomerAutomaticIndirectTaxValidateLocation|string A per-request flag that indicates when Stripe should validate the customer tax location - defaults to `auto`.

---The customer account's tax exemption status: `none`, `exempt`, or `reverse`. When `reverse`, invoice and receipt PDFs include "Reverse charge".
---@alias stripe.UpdateCoreAccountRequestConfigurationCustomerAutomaticIndirectTaxExempt "exempt"|"none"|"reverse"

---A per-request flag that indicates when Stripe should validate the customer tax location - defaults to `auto`.
---@alias stripe.UpdateCoreAccountRequestConfigurationCustomerAutomaticIndirectTaxValidateLocation "auto"|"deferred"|"immediately"

---Billing settings - default settings used for this customer in Billing flows such as Invoices and Subscriptions.
