---@class stripe.UpdateDisputeRequest
---@field dispute string Unique identifier for the object.
---@field evidence? stripe.UpdateDisputeRequestEvidence Evidence to upload, to respond to a dispute. Updating any field in the hash will submit all fields in the hash for review. The combined character count of all fields is limited to 150,000.
---@field expand? stripe.UpdateDisputeRequestExpandList Specifies which fields in the response should be expanded.
---@field intended_submission_method? stripe.UpdateDisputeRequestIntendedSubmissionMethod|string Intended submission method for the dispute.
---@field metadata? stripe.UpdateDisputeRequestMetadata Set of [key-value pairs](https://docs.stripe.com/api/metadata) that you can attach to an object. This can be useful for storing additional information about the object in a structured format. Individual keys can be unset by posting an empty value to them. All keys can be unset by posting an empty value to `metadata`.
---@field submit? boolean Whether to immediately submit evidence to the bank. If `false`, evidence is staged on the dispute. Staged evidence is visible in the API and Dashboard, and can be submitted to the bank by making another request with this attribute set to `true` (the default).
---@field idempotencyKey? string A unique key (up to 255 characters, for example a V4 UUID) that makes a retry of this request safe: Stripe returns the first result for a repeated key instead of performing the operation twice. See https://docs.stripe.com/api/idempotent_requests.

---Evidence to upload, to respond to a dispute. Updating any field in the hash will submit all fields in the hash for review. The combined character count of all fields is limited to 150,000.
---@class stripe.UpdateDisputeRequestEvidence
---@field access_activity_log? string Any server or activity logs showing proof that the customer accessed or downloaded the purchased digital product. This information should include IP addresses, corresponding timestamps, and any detailed recorded activity. Has a maximum character count of 20,000.
---@field appeal? stripe.UpdateDisputeRequestEvidenceAppeal Evidence to submit when appealing a dispute.
---@field billing_address? string The billing address provided by the customer.
---@field cancellation_policy? string (ID of a [file upload](https://stripe.com/docs/guides/file-upload)) Your subscription cancellation policy, as shown to the customer.
---@field cancellation_policy_disclosure? string An explanation of how and when the customer was shown your refund policy prior to purchase. Has a maximum character count of 20,000.
---@field cancellation_rebuttal? string A justification for why the customer's subscription was not canceled. Has a maximum character count of 20,000.
---@field customer_communication? string (ID of a [file upload](https://stripe.com/docs/guides/file-upload)) Any communication with the customer that you feel is relevant to your case. Examples include emails proving that the customer received the product or service, or demonstrating their use of or satisfaction with the product or service.
---@field customer_email_address? string The email address of the customer.
---@field customer_name? string The name of the customer.
---@field customer_purchase_ip? string The IP address that the customer used when making the purchase.
---@field customer_signature? string (ID of a [file upload](https://stripe.com/docs/guides/file-upload)) A relevant document or contract showing the customer's signature.
---@field duplicate_charge_documentation? string (ID of a [file upload](https://stripe.com/docs/guides/file-upload)) Documentation for the prior charge that can uniquely identify the charge, such as a receipt, shipping label, work order, etc. This document should be paired with a similar document from the disputed payment that proves the two payments are separate.
---@field duplicate_charge_explanation? string An explanation of the difference between the disputed charge versus the prior charge that appears to be a duplicate. Has a maximum character count of 20,000.
---@field duplicate_charge_id? string The Stripe ID for the prior charge which appears to be a duplicate of the disputed charge.
---@field enhanced_evidence? stripe.UpdateDisputeRequestEvidenceEnhancedEvidence Additional evidence for qualifying evidence programs.
---@field product_description? string A description of the product or service that was sold. Has a maximum character count of 20,000.
---@field receipt? string (ID of a [file upload](https://stripe.com/docs/guides/file-upload)) Any receipt or message sent to the customer notifying them of the charge.
---@field refund_policy? string (ID of a [file upload](https://stripe.com/docs/guides/file-upload)) Your refund policy, as shown to the customer.
---@field refund_policy_disclosure? string Documentation demonstrating that the customer was shown your refund policy prior to purchase. Has a maximum character count of 20,000.
---@field refund_refusal_explanation? string A justification for why the customer is not entitled to a refund. Has a maximum character count of 20,000.
---@field service_date? string The date on which the customer received or began receiving the purchased service, in a clear human-readable format.
---@field service_documentation? string (ID of a [file upload](https://stripe.com/docs/guides/file-upload)) Documentation showing proof that a service was provided to the customer. This could include a copy of a signed contract, work order, or other form of written agreement.
---@field shipping_address? string The address to which a physical product was shipped. You should try to include as complete address information as possible.
---@field shipping_carrier? string The delivery service that shipped a physical product, such as Fedex, UPS, USPS, etc. If multiple carriers were used for this purchase, please separate them with commas.
---@field shipping_date? string The date on which a physical product began its route to the shipping address, in a clear human-readable format.
