---@class stripe.UpdateIssuingCardholderRequest
---@field cardholder string Unique identifier for the object.
---@field billing? stripe.UpdateIssuingCardholderRequestBilling The cardholder's billing address.
---@field company? stripe.UpdateIssuingCardholderRequestCompany Additional information about a `company` cardholder.
---@field email? string The cardholder's email address.
---@field expand? stripe.UpdateIssuingCardholderRequestExpandList Specifies which fields in the response should be expanded.
---@field individual? stripe.UpdateIssuingCardholderRequestIndividual Additional information about an `individual` cardholder.
---@field metadata? stripe.UpdateIssuingCardholderRequestMetadataMap Set of [key-value pairs](https://docs.stripe.com/api/metadata) that you can attach to an object. This can be useful for storing additional information about the object in a structured format. Individual keys can be unset by posting an empty value to them. All keys can be unset by posting an empty value to `metadata`.
---@field phone_number? string The cardholder's phone number. This is required for all cardholders who will be creating EU cards. See the [3D Secure documentation](https://docs.stripe.com/issuing/3d-secure) for more details.
---@field preferred_locales? stripe.UpdateIssuingCardholderRequestPreferredLocalesList The cardholder’s preferred locales (languages), ordered by preference. Locales can be `de`, `en`, `es`, `fr`, or `it`. This changes the language of the [3D Secure flow](https://docs.stripe.com/issuing/3d-secure) and one-time password messages sent to the cardholder.
---@field spending_controls? stripe.UpdateIssuingCardholderRequestSpendingControls Rules that control spending across this cardholder's cards. Refer to our [documentation](https://docs.stripe.com/issuing/controls/spending-controls) for more details.
---@field status? stripe.UpdateIssuingCardholderRequestStatus|string Specifies whether to permit authorizations on this cardholder's cards.
---@field idempotencyKey? string A unique key (up to 255 characters, for example a V4 UUID) that makes a retry of this request safe: Stripe returns the first result for a repeated key instead of performing the operation twice. See https://docs.stripe.com/api/idempotent_requests.

---The cardholder's billing address.
---@class stripe.UpdateIssuingCardholderRequestBilling
---@field address stripe.UpdateIssuingCardholderRequestBillingAddress The cardholder’s billing address.

---The cardholder’s billing address.
---@class stripe.UpdateIssuingCardholderRequestBillingAddress
---@field city string City, district, suburb, town, or village.
---@field country string Two-letter country code ([ISO 3166-1 alpha-2](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISO_3166-1_alpha-2)).
---@field line1 string Address line 1, such as the street, PO Box, or company name.
---@field line2? string Address line 2, such as the apartment, suite, unit, or building.
---@field postal_code string ZIP or postal code.
---@field state? string State, county, province, or region ([ISO 3166-2](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISO_3166-2)).

---Additional information about a `company` cardholder.
---@class stripe.UpdateIssuingCardholderRequestCompany
