---@class stripe.UpdateIssuingDisputeRequest
---@field dispute string Unique identifier for the object.
---@field amount? number The dispute amount in the card's currency and in the [smallest currency unit](https://docs.stripe.com/currencies#zero-decimal).
---@field evidence? stripe.UpdateIssuingDisputeRequestEvidence Evidence provided for the dispute.
---@field expand? stripe.UpdateIssuingDisputeRequestExpandList Specifies which fields in the response should be expanded.
---@field metadata? stripe.UpdateIssuingDisputeRequestMetadata Set of [key-value pairs](https://docs.stripe.com/api/metadata) that you can attach to an object. This can be useful for storing additional information about the object in a structured format. Individual keys can be unset by posting an empty value to them. All keys can be unset by posting an empty value to `metadata`.
---@field idempotencyKey? string A unique key (up to 255 characters, for example a V4 UUID) that makes a retry of this request safe: Stripe returns the first result for a repeated key instead of performing the operation twice. See https://docs.stripe.com/api/idempotent_requests.

---Evidence provided for the dispute.
---@class stripe.UpdateIssuingDisputeRequestEvidence
---@field canceled? stripe.UpdateIssuingDisputeRequestEvidenceCanceled Evidence provided when `reason` is 'canceled'.
---@field duplicate? stripe.UpdateIssuingDisputeRequestEvidenceDuplicate Evidence provided when `reason` is 'duplicate'.
---@field fraudulent? stripe.UpdateIssuingDisputeRequestEvidenceFraudulent Evidence provided when `reason` is 'fraudulent'.
---@field merchandise_not_as_described? stripe.UpdateIssuingDisputeRequestEvidenceMerchandiseNotAsDescribed Evidence provided when `reason` is 'merchandise_not_as_described'.
