---@field enforce_arithmetic_validation? boolean Set to `false` to return arithmetic validation errors in the response without failing the request. Use this when you want the operation to proceed regardless of arithmetic errors in the line item data. Omit or set to `true` to immediately return a 400 error when arithmetic validation fails. Use this for strict validation that prevents processing with line item data that has arithmetic inconsistencies. For card payments, Stripe doesn't send line item data to card networks if there's an arithmetic validation error.
