---Configuration for any card payments attempted on this PaymentIntent.
---@alias stripe.UpdatePaymentIntentRequestPaymentMethodOptionsCard stripe.UpdatePaymentIntentRequestPaymentMethodOptionsCardCase0|stripe.UpdatePaymentIntentRequestPaymentMethodOptionsCardCase1|string

---@class stripe.UpdatePaymentIntentRequestPaymentMethodOptionsCardCase0
---@field capture_method? stripe.UpdatePaymentIntentRequestPaymentMethodOptionsCardCase0CaptureMethod|string Controls when the funds are captured from the customer's account. If provided, this parameter overrides the behavior of the top-level [capture_method](/api/payment_intents/update#update_payment_intent-capture_method) for this payment method type when finalizing the payment with this payment method type. If `capture_method` is already set on the PaymentIntent, providing an empty value for this parameter unsets the stored value for this payment method type.
---@field cvc_token? string A single-use `cvc_update` Token that represents a card CVC value. When provided, the CVC value will be verified during the card payment attempt. This parameter can only be provided during confirmation.
---@field installments? stripe.UpdatePaymentIntentRequestPaymentMethodOptionsCardCase0Installments Installment configuration for payments attempted on this PaymentIntent. For more information, see the [installments integration guide](https://docs.stripe.com/payments/installments).
---@field mandate_options? stripe.UpdatePaymentIntentRequestPaymentMethodOptionsCardCase0MandateOptions Configuration options for setting up an eMandate for cards issued in India.
---@field moto? boolean When specified, this parameter indicates that a transaction will be marked as MOTO (Mail Order Telephone Order) and thus out of scope for SCA. This parameter can only be provided during confirmation.
---@field network? stripe.UpdatePaymentIntentRequestPaymentMethodOptionsCardCase0Network|string Selected network to process this PaymentIntent on. Depends on the available networks of the card attached to the PaymentIntent. Can be only set confirm-time.
---@field request_extended_authorization? stripe.UpdatePaymentIntentRequestPaymentMethodOptionsCardCase0RequestExtendedAuthorization|string Request ability to [capture beyond the standard authorization validity window](https://docs.stripe.com/payments/extended-authorization) for this PaymentIntent.
---@field request_incremental_authorization? stripe.UpdatePaymentIntentRequestPaymentMethodOptionsCardCase0RequestIncrementalAuthorization|string Request ability to [increment the authorization](https://docs.stripe.com/payments/incremental-authorization) for this PaymentIntent.
---@field request_multicapture? stripe.UpdatePaymentIntentRequestPaymentMethodOptionsCardCase0RequestMulticapture|string Request ability to make [multiple captures](https://docs.stripe.com/payments/multicapture) for this PaymentIntent.
---@field request_overcapture? stripe.UpdatePaymentIntentRequestPaymentMethodOptionsCardCase0RequestOvercapture|string Request ability to [overcapture](https://docs.stripe.com/payments/overcapture) for this PaymentIntent.
---@field request_three_d_secure? stripe.UpdatePaymentIntentRequestPaymentMethodOptionsCardCase0RequestThreeDSecure|string We strongly recommend that you rely on our SCA Engine to automatically prompt your customers for authentication based on risk level and [other requirements](https://docs.stripe.com/strong-customer-authentication). However, if you wish to request 3D Secure based on logic from your own fraud engine, provide this option. If not provided, this value defaults to `automatic`. Read our guide on [manually requesting 3D Secure](https://docs.stripe.com/payments/3d-secure/authentication-flow#manual-three-ds) for more information on how this configuration interacts with Radar and our SCA Engine.
---@field require_cvc_recollection? boolean When enabled, using a card that is attached to a customer will require the CVC to be provided again (i.e. using the cvc_token parameter).
---@field setup_credential_usage? stripe.UpdatePaymentIntentRequestPaymentMethodOptionsCardCase0SetupCredentialUsage|string Set to indicate the future transaction type usage for the card being set up.
---@field setup_future_usage? stripe.UpdatePaymentIntentRequestPaymentMethodOptionsCardCase0SetupFutureUsage|string Indicates that you intend to make future payments with this PaymentIntent's payment method. If you provide a Customer with the PaymentIntent, you can use this parameter to [attach the payment method](/payments/save-during-payment) to the Customer after the PaymentIntent is confirmed and the customer completes any required actions. If you don't provide a Customer, you can still [attach](/api/payment_methods/attach) the payment method to a Customer after the transaction completes. If the payment method is `card_present` and isn't a digital wallet, Stripe creates and attaches a [generated_card](/api/charges/object#charge_object-payment_method_details-card_present-generated_card) payment method representing the card to the Customer instead. When processing card payments, Stripe uses `setup_future_usage` to help you comply with regional legislation and network rules, such as [SCA](/strong-customer-authentication). If you've already set `setup_future_usage` and you're performing a request using a publishable key, you can only update the value from `on_session` to `off_session`.
---@field statement_descriptor_suffix_kana? stripe.UpdatePaymentIntentRequestPaymentMethodOptionsCardCase0StatementDescriptorSuffixKana Provides information about a card payment that customers see on their statements. Concatenated with the Kana prefix (shortened Kana descriptor) or Kana statement descriptor that’s set on the account to form the complete statement descriptor. Maximum 22 characters. On card statements, the *concatenation* of both prefix and suffix (including separators) will appear truncated to 22 characters.
---@field statement_descriptor_suffix_kanji? stripe.UpdatePaymentIntentRequestPaymentMethodOptionsCardCase0StatementDescriptorSuffixKanji Provides information about a card payment that customers see on their statements. Concatenated with the Kanji prefix (shortened Kanji descriptor) or Kanji statement descriptor that’s set on the account to form the complete statement descriptor. Maximum 17 characters. On card statements, the *concatenation* of both prefix and suffix (including separators) will appear truncated to 17 characters.
---@field stored_credential_usage? stripe.UpdatePaymentIntentRequestPaymentMethodOptionsCardCase0StoredCredentialUsage|string Use this parameter in scenarios where you collect card details and [charge them later](https://stripe.com/docs/payments/cards/charging-saved-cards). When making an off session payment with a previously saved card (that was saved with a SetupIntent or with a PaymentIntent with `setup_future_usage`), set this parameter to indicate the type of transaction. You can set this parameter at any time before or during PaymentIntent confirmation, and confirm this PaymentIntent with `off_session=true`. Note that this parameter is currently unsupported with the `setup_future_usage` parameter.
---@field three_d_secure? stripe.UpdatePaymentIntentRequestPaymentMethodOptionsCardCase0ThreeDSecure If 3D Secure authentication was performed with a third-party provider, the authentication details to use for this payment.

