---@class stripe.UpdatePaymentMethodDomainRequest
---@field payment_method_domain string Unique identifier for the object.
---@field enabled? boolean Whether this payment method domain is enabled. If the domain is not enabled, payment methods that require a payment method domain will not appear in Elements or Embedded Checkout.
---@field expand? stripe.UpdatePaymentMethodDomainRequestExpandList Specifies which fields in the response should be expanded.
---@field idempotencyKey? string A unique key (up to 255 characters, for example a V4 UUID) that makes a retry of this request safe: Stripe returns the first result for a repeated key instead of performing the operation twice. See https://docs.stripe.com/api/idempotent_requests.

---Specifies which fields in the response should be expanded.
---@alias stripe.UpdatePaymentMethodDomainRequestExpandList string[]

---@class stripe.UpdatePaymentMethodRequest
---@field payment_method string Unique identifier for the object.
---@field allow_redisplay? stripe.UpdatePaymentMethodRequestAllowRedisplay|string This field indicates whether this payment method can be shown again to its customer in a checkout flow. Stripe products such as Checkout and Elements use this field to determine whether a payment method can be shown as a saved payment method in a checkout flow. The field defaults to `unspecified`.
---@field billing_details? stripe.UpdatePaymentMethodRequestBillingDetails Billing information associated with the PaymentMethod that may be used or required by particular types of payment methods.
---@field card? stripe.UpdatePaymentMethodRequestCard If this is a `card` PaymentMethod, this hash contains the user's card details.
---@field expand? stripe.UpdatePaymentMethodRequestExpandList Specifies which fields in the response should be expanded.
---@field metadata? stripe.UpdatePaymentMethodRequestMetadata Set of [key-value pairs](https://docs.stripe.com/api/metadata) that you can attach to an object. This can be useful for storing additional information about the object in a structured format. Individual keys can be unset by posting an empty value to them. All keys can be unset by posting an empty value to `metadata`.
---@field us_bank_account? stripe.UpdatePaymentMethodRequestUsBankAccount If this is an `us_bank_account` PaymentMethod, this hash contains details about the US bank account payment method.
---@field idempotencyKey? string A unique key (up to 255 characters, for example a V4 UUID) that makes a retry of this request safe: Stripe returns the first result for a repeated key instead of performing the operation twice. See https://docs.stripe.com/api/idempotent_requests.

---This field indicates whether this payment method can be shown again to its customer in a checkout flow. Stripe products such as Checkout and Elements use this field to determine whether a payment method can be shown as a saved payment method in a checkout flow. The field defaults to `unspecified`.
---@alias stripe.UpdatePaymentMethodRequestAllowRedisplay "always"|"limited"|"unspecified"

