---Information about a mandate possibility attached to a source object (generally for bank debits) as well as its acceptance status.
---@class stripe.UpdateSourceRequestMandate
---@field acceptance? stripe.UpdateSourceRequestMandateAcceptance The parameters required to notify Stripe of a mandate acceptance or refusal by the customer.
---@field amount? stripe.UpdateSourceRequestMandateAmount The amount specified by the mandate. (Leave null for a mandate covering all amounts)
---@field currency? string The currency specified by the mandate. (Must match `currency` of the source)
---@field interval? stripe.UpdateSourceRequestMandateInterval|string The interval of debits permitted by the mandate. Either `one_time` (just permitting a single debit), `scheduled` (with debits on an agreed schedule or for clearly-defined events), or `variable`(for debits with any frequency)
---@field notification_method? stripe.UpdateSourceRequestMandateNotificationMethod|string The method Stripe should use to notify the customer of upcoming debit instructions and/or mandate confirmation as required by the underlying debit network. Either `email` (an email is sent directly to the customer), `manual` (a `source.mandate_notification` event is sent to your webhooks endpoint and you should handle the notification) or `none` (the underlying debit network does not require any notification).

---The parameters required to notify Stripe of a mandate acceptance or refusal by the customer.
---@class stripe.UpdateSourceRequestMandateAcceptance
---@field date? number The Unix timestamp (in seconds) when the mandate was accepted or refused by the customer.
---@field ip? string The IP address from which the mandate was accepted or refused by the customer.
---@field offline? stripe.UpdateSourceRequestMandateAcceptanceOffline The parameters required to store a mandate accepted offline. Should only be set if `mandate[type]` is `offline`
---@field online? stripe.UpdateSourceRequestMandateAcceptanceOnline The parameters required to store a mandate accepted online. Should only be set if `mandate[type]` is `online`
---@field status stripe.UpdateSourceRequestMandateAcceptanceStatus|string The status of the mandate acceptance. Either `accepted` (the mandate was accepted) or `refused` (the mandate was refused).
---@field type? stripe.UpdateSourceRequestMandateAcceptanceType|string The type of acceptance information included with the mandate. Either `online` or `offline`
---@field user_agent? string The user agent of the browser from which the mandate was accepted or refused by the customer.

---The parameters required to store a mandate accepted offline. Should only be set if `mandate[type]` is `offline`
---@class stripe.UpdateSourceRequestMandateAcceptanceOffline
---@field contact_email string An email to contact you with if a copy of the mandate is requested, required if `type` is `offline`.

---The parameters required to store a mandate accepted online. Should only be set if `mandate[type]` is `online`
---@class stripe.UpdateSourceRequestMandateAcceptanceOnline
---@field date? number The Unix timestamp (in seconds) when the mandate was accepted or refused by the customer.
---@field ip? string The IP address from which the mandate was accepted or refused by the customer.
