---@class stripe.UpdateSubscriptionItemRequest
---@field item string Unique identifier for the object.
---@field billing_thresholds? stripe.UpdateSubscriptionItemRequestBillingThresholds Define thresholds at which an invoice will be sent, and the subscription advanced to a new billing period. Pass an empty string to remove previously-defined thresholds.
---@field current_trial? stripe.UpdateSubscriptionItemRequestCurrentTrial The trial offer to apply to this subscription item.
---@field discounts? stripe.UpdateSubscriptionItemRequestDiscounts The coupons to redeem into discounts for the subscription item.
---@field expand? stripe.UpdateSubscriptionItemRequestExpandList Specifies which fields in the response should be expanded.
---@field metadata? stripe.UpdateSubscriptionItemRequestMetadata Set of [key-value pairs](https://docs.stripe.com/api/metadata) that you can attach to an object. This can be useful for storing additional information about the object in a structured format. Individual keys can be unset by posting an empty value to them. All keys can be unset by posting an empty value to `metadata`.
---@field off_session? boolean Indicates if a customer is on or off-session while an invoice payment is attempted. Defaults to `false` (on-session).
---@field payment_behavior? stripe.UpdateSubscriptionItemRequestPaymentBehavior|string Controls how Stripe handles payment when a subscription update requires payment and `collection_method=charge_automatically`.
---@field plan? string The identifier of the new plan for this subscription item.
---@field price? string The ID of the price object. You can use either `price` or `price_data`, but not both, to set or change this item's price. If you're updating an existing item without changing its price, omit both. When changing a subscription item's price, `quantity` is set to 1 unless a `quantity` parameter is provided.
---@field price_data? stripe.UpdateSubscriptionItemRequestPriceData Data used to generate a new [Price](https://docs.stripe.com/api/prices) object inline. You can use either `price` or `price_data`, but not both, to set or change this item's price. If you're updating an existing item without changing its price, omit both.
---@field proration_behavior? stripe.UpdateSubscriptionItemRequestProrationBehavior|string Determines how to handle [prorations](https://docs.stripe.com/billing/subscriptions/prorations) when the billing cycle changes (e.g., when switching plans, resetting `billing_cycle_anchor=now`, or starting a trial), or if an item's `quantity` changes. The default value is `create_prorations`.
---@field proration_date? number If set, the proration will be calculated as though the subscription was updated at the given time. This can be used to apply the same proration that was previewed with the [upcoming invoice](/api/invoices/create_preview) endpoint.
---@field quantity? number The quantity you'd like to apply to the subscription item you're creating.
---@field tax_rates? stripe.UpdateSubscriptionItemRequestTaxRates A list of [Tax Rate](https://docs.stripe.com/api/tax_rates) ids. These Tax Rates will override the [`default_tax_rates`](https://docs.stripe.com/api/subscriptions/create#create_subscription-default_tax_rates) on the Subscription. When updating, pass an empty string to remove previously-defined tax rates.
---@field idempotencyKey? string A unique key (up to 255 characters, for example a V4 UUID) that makes a retry of this request safe: Stripe returns the first result for a repeated key instead of performing the operation twice. See https://docs.stripe.com/api/idempotent_requests.

