---Controls how Stripe handles payment when a subscription update requires payment and `collection_method=charge_automatically`.
---@alias stripe.UpdateSubscriptionItemRequestPaymentBehavior "allow_incomplete"|"default_incomplete"|"error_if_incomplete"|"pending_if_incomplete"

---Data used to generate a new [Price](https://docs.stripe.com/api/prices) object inline. You can use either `price` or `price_data`, but not both, to set or change this item's price. If you're updating an existing item without changing its price, omit both.
---@class stripe.UpdateSubscriptionItemRequestPriceData
---@field currency string Three-letter [ISO currency code](https://www.iso.org/iso-4217-currency-codes.html), in lowercase. Must be a [supported currency](https://stripe.com/docs/currencies).
---@field product string The ID of the [Product](https://docs.stripe.com/api/products) that this [Price](https://docs.stripe.com/api/prices) will belong to.
---@field recurring stripe.UpdateSubscriptionItemRequestPriceDataRecurring The recurring components of a price such as `interval` and `interval_count`.
---@field tax_behavior? stripe.UpdateSubscriptionItemRequestPriceDataTaxBehavior|string Only required if a [default tax behavior](https://docs.stripe.com/tax/products-prices-tax-categories-tax-behavior#setting-a-default-tax-behavior-(recommended)) was not provided in the Stripe Tax settings. Specifies whether the price is considered inclusive of taxes or exclusive of taxes. One of `inclusive`, `exclusive`, or `unspecified`. Once specified as either `inclusive` or `exclusive`, it cannot be changed.
---@field unit_amount? number A positive integer in cents (or local equivalent) (or 0 for a free price) representing how much to charge.
---@field unit_amount_decimal? string Same as `unit_amount`, but accepts a decimal value in cents (or local equivalent) with at most 12 decimal places. Only one of `unit_amount` and `unit_amount_decimal` can be set.

---The recurring components of a price such as `interval` and `interval_count`.
---@class stripe.UpdateSubscriptionItemRequestPriceDataRecurring
---@field interval stripe.UpdateSubscriptionItemRequestPriceDataRecurringInterval|string Specifies billing frequency. Either `day`, `week`, `month` or `year`.
---@field interval_count? number The number of intervals between subscription billings. For example, `interval=month` and `interval_count=3` bills every 3 months. Maximum of three years interval allowed (3 years, 36 months, or 156 weeks).

---Specifies billing frequency. Either `day`, `week`, `month` or `year`.
---@alias stripe.UpdateSubscriptionItemRequestPriceDataRecurringInterval "day"|"month"|"week"|"year"

---Only required if a [default tax behavior](https://docs.stripe.com/tax/products-prices-tax-categories-tax-behavior#setting-a-default-tax-behavior-(recommended)) was not provided in the Stripe Tax settings. Specifies whether the price is considered inclusive of taxes or exclusive of taxes. One of `inclusive`, `exclusive`, or `unspecified`. Once specified as either `inclusive` or `exclusive`, it cannot be changed.
---@alias stripe.UpdateSubscriptionItemRequestPriceDataTaxBehavior "exclusive"|"inclusive"|"unspecified"

---Determines how to handle [prorations](https://docs.stripe.com/billing/subscriptions/prorations) when the billing cycle changes (e.g., when switching plans, resetting `billing_cycle_anchor=now`, or starting a trial), or if an item's `quantity` changes. The default value is `create_prorations`.
---@alias stripe.UpdateSubscriptionItemRequestProrationBehavior "always_invoice"|"create_prorations"|"none"

---A list of [Tax Rate](https://docs.stripe.com/api/tax_rates) ids. These Tax Rates will override the [`default_tax_rates`](https://docs.stripe.com/api/subscriptions/create#create_subscription-default_tax_rates) on the Subscription. When updating, pass an empty string to remove previously-defined tax rates.
