---@class stripe.UpdateSubscriptionScheduleRequest
---@field schedule string
---@field default_settings? stripe.UpdateSubscriptionScheduleRequestDefaultSettings Object representing the subscription schedule's default settings.
---@field end_behavior? stripe.UpdateSubscriptionScheduleRequestEndBehavior|string Behavior of the subscription schedule and underlying subscription when it ends. Possible values are `release` or `cancel` with the default being `release`. `release` will end the subscription schedule and keep the underlying subscription running. `cancel` will end the subscription schedule and cancel the underlying subscription.
---@field expand? stripe.UpdateSubscriptionScheduleRequestExpandList Specifies which fields in the response should be expanded.
---@field metadata? stripe.UpdateSubscriptionScheduleRequestMetadata Set of [key-value pairs](https://docs.stripe.com/api/metadata) that you can attach to an object. This can be useful for storing additional information about the object in a structured format. Individual keys can be unset by posting an empty value to them. All keys can be unset by posting an empty value to `metadata`.
---@field pause_schedules? stripe.UpdateSubscriptionScheduleRequestPauseSchedules The subscription's pause behavior and optional resume behavior. You can provide one entry. Include its `key` to update an existing pause schedule. Omit `pause_schedules` to leave the existing schedule unchanged, or pass an empty string (`""`) to clear it.
---@field phases? stripe.UpdateSubscriptionScheduleRequestPhasesList List representing phases of the subscription schedule. Each phase can be customized to have different durations, plans, and coupons. If there are multiple phases, the `end_date` of one phase will always equal the `start_date` of the next phase. Note that past phases can be omitted.
---@field proration_behavior? stripe.UpdateSubscriptionScheduleRequestProrationBehavior|string If the update changes the billing configuration (item price, quantity, etc.) of the current phase, indicates how prorations from this change should be handled. The default value is `create_prorations`.
---@field idempotencyKey? string A unique key (up to 255 characters, for example a V4 UUID) that makes a retry of this request safe: Stripe returns the first result for a repeated key instead of performing the operation twice. See https://docs.stripe.com/api/idempotent_requests.

---Object representing the subscription schedule's default settings.
---@class stripe.UpdateSubscriptionScheduleRequestDefaultSettings
---@field application_fee_percent? number A non-negative decimal between 0 and 100, with at most two decimal places. This represents the percentage of the subscription invoice total that will be transferred to the application owner's Stripe account. The request must be made by a platform account on a connected account in order to set an application fee percentage. For more information, see the application fees [documentation](https://stripe.com/docs/connect/subscriptions#collecting-fees-on-subscriptions).
---@field automatic_tax? stripe.UpdateSubscriptionScheduleRequestDefaultSettingsAutomaticTax Default settings for automatic tax computation.
---@field billing_cycle_anchor? stripe.UpdateSubscriptionScheduleRequestDefaultSettingsBillingCycleAnchor|string Can be set to `phase_start` to set the anchor to the start of the phase or `automatic` to automatically change it if needed. Cannot be set to `phase_start` if this phase specifies a trial. For more information, see the billing cycle [documentation](https://docs.stripe.com/billing/subscriptions/billing-cycle).
---@field billing_thresholds? stripe.UpdateSubscriptionScheduleRequestDefaultSettingsBillingThresholds Define thresholds at which an invoice will be sent, and the subscription advanced to a new billing period. Pass an empty string to remove previously-defined thresholds.
---@field collection_method? stripe.UpdateSubscriptionScheduleRequestDefaultSettingsCollectionMethod|string Either `charge_automatically`, or `send_invoice`. When charging automatically, Stripe will attempt to pay the underlying subscription at the end of each billing cycle using the default source attached to the customer. When sending an invoice, Stripe will email your customer an invoice with payment instructions and mark the subscription as `active`. Defaults to `charge_automatically` on creation.
---@field default_payment_method? string ID of the default payment method for the subscription schedule. It must belong to the customer associated with the subscription schedule. If not set, invoices will use the default payment method in the customer's invoice settings.
---@field description? stripe.UpdateSubscriptionScheduleRequestDefaultSettingsDescription Subscription description, meant to be displayable to the customer. Use this field to optionally store an explanation of the subscription for rendering in Stripe surfaces and certain local payment methods UIs.
---@field invoice_settings? stripe.UpdateSubscriptionScheduleRequestDefaultSettingsInvoiceSettings All invoices will be billed using the specified settings.
---@field on_behalf_of? stripe.UpdateSubscriptionScheduleRequestDefaultSettingsOnBehalfOf The account on behalf of which to charge, for each of the associated subscription's invoices.
---@field transfer_data? stripe.UpdateSubscriptionScheduleRequestDefaultSettingsTransferData The data with which to automatically create a Transfer for each of the associated subscription's invoices.

---Default settings for automatic tax computation.
---@class stripe.UpdateSubscriptionScheduleRequestDefaultSettingsAutomaticTax
---@field enabled boolean Enabled automatic tax calculation which will automatically compute tax rates on all invoices generated by the subscription.
