---@class stripe.UpdateSubscriptionScheduleRequestPhasesItem
---@field add_invoice_items? stripe.UpdateSubscriptionScheduleRequestPhasesItemAddInvoiceItemsList A list of prices and quantities that will generate invoice items appended to the next invoice for this phase. You may pass up to 20 items.
---@field application_fee_percent? number A non-negative decimal between 0 and 100, with at most two decimal places. This represents the percentage of the subscription invoice total that will be transferred to the application owner's Stripe account. The request must be made by a platform account on a connected account in order to set an application fee percentage. For more information, see the application fees [documentation](https://stripe.com/docs/connect/subscriptions#collecting-fees-on-subscriptions).
---@field automatic_tax? stripe.UpdateSubscriptionScheduleRequestPhasesItemAutomaticTax Automatic tax settings for this phase.
---@field billing_cycle_anchor? stripe.UpdateSubscriptionScheduleRequestPhasesItemBillingCycleAnchor|string Can be set to `phase_start` to set the anchor to the start of the phase or `automatic` to automatically change it if needed. Cannot be set to `phase_start` if this phase specifies a trial. For more information, see the billing cycle [documentation](https://docs.stripe.com/billing/subscriptions/billing-cycle).
---@field billing_thresholds? stripe.UpdateSubscriptionScheduleRequestPhasesItemBillingThresholds Define thresholds at which an invoice will be sent, and the subscription advanced to a new billing period. Pass an empty string to remove previously-defined thresholds.
---@field collection_method? stripe.UpdateSubscriptionScheduleRequestPhasesItemCollectionMethod|string Either `charge_automatically`, or `send_invoice`. When charging automatically, Stripe will attempt to pay the underlying subscription at the end of each billing cycle using the default source attached to the customer. When sending an invoice, Stripe will email your customer an invoice with payment instructions and mark the subscription as `active`. Defaults to `charge_automatically` on creation.
---@field currency? string Three-letter [ISO currency code](https://www.iso.org/iso-4217-currency-codes.html), in lowercase. Must be a [supported currency](https://stripe.com/docs/currencies).
---@field default_payment_method? string ID of the default payment method for the subscription schedule. It must belong to the customer associated with the subscription schedule. If not set, invoices will use the default payment method in the customer's invoice settings.
---@field default_tax_rates? stripe.UpdateSubscriptionScheduleRequestPhasesItemDefaultTaxRates A list of [Tax Rate](https://docs.stripe.com/api/tax_rates) ids. These Tax Rates will set the Subscription's [`default_tax_rates`](https://docs.stripe.com/api/subscriptions/create#create_subscription-default_tax_rates), which means they will be the Invoice's [`default_tax_rates`](https://docs.stripe.com/api/invoices/create#create_invoice-default_tax_rates) for any Invoices issued by the Subscription during this Phase.
---@field description? stripe.UpdateSubscriptionScheduleRequestPhasesItemDescription Subscription description, meant to be displayable to the customer. Use this field to optionally store an explanation of the subscription for rendering in Stripe surfaces and certain local payment methods UIs.
---@field discounts? stripe.UpdateSubscriptionScheduleRequestPhasesItemDiscounts The coupons to redeem into discounts for the schedule phase. If not specified, inherits the discount from the subscription's customer. Pass an empty string to avoid inheriting any discounts.
---@field duration? stripe.UpdateSubscriptionScheduleRequestPhasesItemDuration The number of intervals the phase should last. If set, `end_date` must not be set.
---@field end_date? stripe.UpdateSubscriptionScheduleRequestPhasesItemEndDate The date at which this phase of the subscription schedule ends. If set, `duration` must not be set.
---@field invoice_settings? stripe.UpdateSubscriptionScheduleRequestPhasesItemInvoiceSettings All invoices will be billed using the specified settings.
---@field items stripe.UpdateSubscriptionScheduleRequestPhasesItemItemsList List of configuration items, each with an attached price, to apply during this phase of the subscription schedule.
---@field metadata? stripe.UpdateSubscriptionScheduleRequestPhasesItemMetadataMap Set of [key-value pairs](https://docs.stripe.com/api/metadata) that you can attach to a phase. Metadata on a schedule's phase will update the underlying subscription's `metadata` when the phase is entered, adding new keys and replacing existing keys in the subscription's `metadata`. Individual keys in the subscription's `metadata` can be unset by posting an empty value to them in the phase's `metadata`. To unset all keys in the subscription's `metadata`, update the subscription directly or unset every key individually from the phase's `metadata`.
---@field on_behalf_of? string The account on behalf of which to charge, for each of the associated subscription's invoices.
---@field proration_behavior? stripe.UpdateSubscriptionScheduleRequestPhasesItemProrationBehavior|string Controls whether the subscription schedule should create [prorations](https://docs.stripe.com/billing/subscriptions/prorations) when transitioning to this phase if there is a difference in billing configuration. It's different from the request-level [proration_behavior](https://docs.stripe.com/api/subscription_schedules/update#update_subscription_schedule-proration_behavior) parameter which controls what happens if the update request affects the billing configuration (item price, quantity, etc.) of the current phase.
---@field start_date? stripe.UpdateSubscriptionScheduleRequestPhasesItemStartDate The date at which this phase of the subscription schedule starts or `now`. Must be set on the first phase. Prefer to specify `now` over an explicit timestamp when appropriate to avoid unexpected behavior due to request delays or clock skew resulting in the phase being slightly backdated or postdated.
---@field transfer_data? stripe.UpdateSubscriptionScheduleRequestPhasesItemTransferData The data with which to automatically create a Transfer for each of the associated subscription's invoices.
---@field trial? boolean If set to true the entire phase is counted as a trial and the customer will not be charged for any fees.
---@field trial_end? stripe.UpdateSubscriptionScheduleRequestPhasesItemTrialEnd Sets the phase to trialing from the start date to this date. Must be within the phase. When combined with `trial=true`, it must match the phase end date.

---@class stripe.UpdateSubscriptionScheduleRequestPhasesItemAddInvoiceItemsItem
---@field discountable? boolean Controls whether discounts apply to this invoice item. Defaults to true if no value is provided.
---@field discounts? stripe.UpdateSubscriptionScheduleRequestPhasesItemAddInvoiceItemsItemDiscountsList The coupons to redeem into discounts for the item.
---@field metadata? stripe.UpdateSubscriptionScheduleRequestPhasesItemAddInvoiceItemsItemMetadataMap Set of [key-value pairs](https://docs.stripe.com/api/metadata) that you can attach to an object. This can be useful for storing additional information about the object in a structured format. Individual keys can be unset by posting an empty value to them. All keys can be unset by posting an empty value to `metadata`.
---@field period? stripe.UpdateSubscriptionScheduleRequestPhasesItemAddInvoiceItemsItemPeriod The period associated with this invoice item. If not set, `period.start.type` defaults to `max_item_period_start` and `period.end.type` defaults to `min_item_period_end`.
---@field price? string The ID of the price object. One of `price` or `price_data` is required.
---@field price_data? stripe.UpdateSubscriptionScheduleRequestPhasesItemAddInvoiceItemsItemPriceData Data used to generate a new [Price](https://docs.stripe.com/api/prices) object inline. One of `price` or `price_data` is required.
---@field quantity? number Quantity for this item. Defaults to 1.
---@field tax_rates? stripe.UpdateSubscriptionScheduleRequestPhasesItemAddInvoiceItemsItemTaxRates The tax rates which apply to the item. When set, the `default_tax_rates` do not apply to this item.

