---@class stripe.UpdateTerminalLocationRequest
---@field location string Unique identifier for the object.
---@field address? stripe.UpdateTerminalLocationRequestAddress The full address of the location. You can't change the location's `country`. If you need to modify the `country` field, create a new `Location` object and re-register any existing readers to that location.
---@field address_kana? stripe.UpdateTerminalLocationRequestAddressKana The Kana variation of the full address of the location (Japan only).
---@field address_kanji? stripe.UpdateTerminalLocationRequestAddressKanji The Kanji variation of the full address of the location (Japan only).
---@field configuration_overrides? stripe.UpdateTerminalLocationRequestConfigurationOverrides The ID of a configuration that will be used to customize all readers in this location.
---@field display_name? stripe.UpdateTerminalLocationRequestDisplayName A name for the location.
---@field display_name_kana? stripe.UpdateTerminalLocationRequestDisplayNameKana The Kana variation of the name for the location (Japan only).
---@field display_name_kanji? stripe.UpdateTerminalLocationRequestDisplayNameKanji The Kanji variation of the name for the location (Japan only).
---@field expand? stripe.UpdateTerminalLocationRequestExpandList Specifies which fields in the response should be expanded.
---@field metadata? stripe.UpdateTerminalLocationRequestMetadata Set of [key-value pairs](https://docs.stripe.com/api/metadata) that you can attach to an object. This can be useful for storing additional information about the object in a structured format. Individual keys can be unset by posting an empty value to them. All keys can be unset by posting an empty value to `metadata`.
---@field phone? stripe.UpdateTerminalLocationRequestPhone The phone number for the location.
---@field idempotencyKey? string A unique key (up to 255 characters, for example a V4 UUID) that makes a retry of this request safe: Stripe returns the first result for a repeated key instead of performing the operation twice. See https://docs.stripe.com/api/idempotent_requests.

---The full address of the location. You can't change the location's `country`. If you need to modify the `country` field, create a new `Location` object and re-register any existing readers to that location.
---@class stripe.UpdateTerminalLocationRequestAddress
---@field city? string City, district, suburb, town, or village.
---@field country? string Two-letter country code ([ISO 3166-1 alpha-2](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISO_3166-1_alpha-2)).
