---A Meter Event is a usage record that captures billable activity for usage-based billing. Meter Events contain an event name, timestamp, and payload with customer mapping and usage value, enabling accurate usage tracking and billing.
---@class stripe.V2BillingMeterEvent
---@field created string The creation time of this meter event.
---@field event_name string The name of the meter event. Corresponds with the `event_name` field on a meter.
---@field identifier string A unique identifier for the event. If not provided, one will be generated. We recommend using a globally unique identifier for this. We'll enforce uniqueness within a rolling 24 hour period.
---@field livemode boolean Has the value `true` if the object exists in live mode or the value `false` if the object exists in test mode.
---@field object stripe.V2BillingMeterEventObject String representing the object's type. Objects of the same type share the same value of the object field.
---@field payload stripe.V2BillingMeterEventPayloadMap The payload of the event. This must contain the fields corresponding to a meter's `customer_mapping.event_payload_key` (default is `stripe_customer_id`) and `value_settings.event_payload_key` (default is `value`). Read more about the [payload](https://docs.stripe.com/billing/subscriptions/usage-based/recording-usage#payload-key-overrides)..
---@field timestamp string The time of the event. Must be within the past 35 calendar days or up to 5 minutes in the future. Defaults to current timestamp if not specified.

---A Meter Event Adjustment is used to cancel or modify previously recorded meter events. Meter Event Adjustments allow you to correct billing data by canceling individual events or event ranges, with tracking of adjustment status and creation time.
---@class stripe.V2BillingMeterEventAdjustment
---@field cancel stripe.V2BillingMeterEventAdjustmentCancel Specifies which event to cancel.
---@field created string The time the adjustment was created.
---@field event_name string The name of the meter event. Corresponds with the `event_name` field on a meter.
---@field id string The unique ID of this meter event adjustment.
---@field livemode boolean Has the value `true` if the object exists in live mode or the value `false` if the object exists in test mode.
---@field object stripe.V2BillingMeterEventAdjustmentObject String representing the object's type. Objects of the same type share the same value of the object field.
---@field status stripe.V2BillingMeterEventAdjustmentStatus Open Enum. The meter event adjustment's status.
---@field type stripe.V2BillingMeterEventAdjustmentType Open Enum. Specifies the type of cancellation. Currently supports canceling a single event.

---Specifies which event to cancel.
---@class stripe.V2BillingMeterEventAdjustmentCancel
---@field identifier string The identifier that was originally assigned to the meter event. You can only cancel events within 24 hours of Stripe receiving them.

