---An Account v2 object represents a company, individual, or other entity that your Stripe integration interacts with. It contains both identifying information and properties that control its behavior and functionality. An Account can have one or more configurations that enable sets of related features, such as allowing it to act as a merchant or customer.
---The Accounts v2 API is broadly available to Connect platforms, and to other users in preview. The Accounts v2 API also supports the Global Payouts preview feature.
---@class stripe.V2CoreAccount
---@field applied_configurations stripe.V2CoreAccountAppliedConfigurationsList The configurations that have been applied to this account.
---@field closed? boolean Indicates whether the account has been closed.
---@field configuration? stripe.V2CoreAccountConfiguration An Account represents a company, individual, or other entity that a user interacts with. Accounts store identity information and one or more configurations that enable product-specific capabilities. You can assign configurations at creation or add them later.
---@field contact_email? string The primary contact email address for the Account.
---@field contact_phone? string The default contact phone for the Account.
---@field created string Time at which the object was created. Represented as a RFC 3339 date & time UTC value in millisecond precision, for example: 2022-09-18T13:22:18.123Z.
---@field dashboard? stripe.V2CoreAccountDashboard A value indicating the Stripe dashboard this Account has access to. This will depend on which configurations are enabled for this account.
---@field defaults? stripe.V2CoreAccountDefaults Default values for settings shared across Account configurations.
---@field display_name? string A descriptive name for the Account. This name will be surfaced in the Stripe Dashboard and on any invoices sent to the Account.
---@field future_requirements? stripe.V2CoreAccountFutureRequirements Information about the future requirements for the Account that will eventually come into effect, including what information needs to be collected, and by when.
---@field id string Unique identifier for the Account.
---@field identity? stripe.V2CoreAccountIdentity Information about the company, individual, and business represented by the Account.
---@field livemode boolean Has the value `true` if the object exists in live mode or the value `false` if the object exists in test mode.
---@field metadata? stripe.V2CoreAccountMetadataMap Set of key-value pairs that you can attach to an object. This can be useful for storing additional information about the object in a structured format.
---@field object stripe.V2CoreAccountObject String representing the object's type. Objects of the same type share the same value of the object field.
---@field requirements? stripe.V2CoreAccountRequirements Information about the active requirements for the Account, including what information needs to be collected, and by when.

---@alias stripe.V2CoreAccountAppliedConfigurationsItem "customer"|"merchant"|"recipient"

---The configurations that have been applied to this account.
---@alias stripe.V2CoreAccountAppliedConfigurationsList stripe.V2CoreAccountAppliedConfigurationsItem[]

---An Account represents a company, individual, or other entity that a user interacts with. Accounts store identity information and one or more configurations that enable product-specific capabilities. You can assign configurations at creation or add them later.
---@class stripe.V2CoreAccountConfiguration
---@field customer? stripe.V2CoreAccountConfigurationCustomer The Customer Configuration allows the Account to be used in inbound payment flows (i.e. customer-facing payment and billing flows).
---@field merchant? stripe.V2CoreAccountConfigurationMerchant Enables the Account to act as a connected account and collect payments facilitated by a Connect platform. You must onboard your platform to Connect before you can add this configuration to your connected accounts. Utilize this configuration when the Account will be the Merchant of Record, like with Direct charges or Destination Charges with on_behalf_of set.
---@field recipient? stripe.V2CoreAccountConfigurationRecipient The Recipient Configuration allows the Account to receive funds. Utilize this configuration if the Account will not be the Merchant of Record, like with Separate Charges & Transfers, or Destination Charges without on_behalf_of set.

---The Customer Configuration allows the Account to be used in inbound payment flows (i.e. customer-facing payment and billing flows).
---@class stripe.V2CoreAccountConfigurationCustomer
---@field applied boolean Indicates whether the customer configuration is active. You can deactivate or reactivate the customer configuration by updating this property. Deactivating the configuration by setting this value to false will unrequest all capabilities within the configuration. It will not delete any of the configuration's other properties.
---@field automatic_indirect_tax? stripe.V2CoreAccountConfigurationCustomerAutomaticIndirectTax Settings for automatic indirect tax calculation on the customer's invoices, subscriptions, Checkout Sessions, and Payment Links. Available when automatic tax calculation is available for the customer account's location.
---@field billing? stripe.V2CoreAccountConfigurationCustomerBilling Default Billing settings for the customer account, used in Invoices and Subscriptions.
---@field capabilities? stripe.V2CoreAccountConfigurationCustomerCapabilities Capabilities that have been requested on the Customer Configuration.
---@field shipping? stripe.V2CoreAccountConfigurationCustomerShipping The customer's shipping information. Appears on invoices emailed to this customer.
---@field test_clock? string ID of the test clock to attach to the customer. Can only be set on testmode Accounts, and when the Customer Configuration is first set on an Account.

---Settings for automatic indirect tax calculation on the customer's invoices, subscriptions, Checkout Sessions, and Payment Links. Available when automatic tax calculation is available for the customer account's location.
---@class stripe.V2CoreAccountConfigurationCustomerAutomaticIndirectTax
---@field exempt? stripe.V2CoreAccountConfigurationCustomerAutomaticIndirectTaxExempt The customer account's tax exemption status: `none`, `exempt`, or `reverse`. When `reverse`, invoice and receipt PDFs include "Reverse charge".
---@field ip_address? string A recent IP address of the customer used for tax reporting and tax location inference.
---@field location? stripe.V2CoreAccountConfigurationCustomerAutomaticIndirectTaxLocation The customer account's identified tax location, derived from `location_source`. Only rendered if the `automatic_indirect_tax` feature is requested and `active`.
---@field location_source? stripe.V2CoreAccountConfigurationCustomerAutomaticIndirectTaxLocationSource Data source used to identify the customer account's tax location. Defaults to `identity_address`. Used for automatic indirect tax calculation.

---The customer account's tax exemption status: `none`, `exempt`, or `reverse`. When `reverse`, invoice and receipt PDFs include "Reverse charge".
---@alias stripe.V2CoreAccountConfigurationCustomerAutomaticIndirectTaxExempt "exempt"|"none"|"reverse"

---The customer account's identified tax location, derived from `location_source`. Only rendered if the `automatic_indirect_tax` feature is requested and `active`.
---@class stripe.V2CoreAccountConfigurationCustomerAutomaticIndirectTaxLocation
---@field country? string The identified tax country of the customer.
---@field state? string The identified tax state, county, province, or region of the customer.

---Data source used to identify the customer account's tax location. Defaults to `identity_address`. Used for automatic indirect tax calculation.
---@alias stripe.V2CoreAccountConfigurationCustomerAutomaticIndirectTaxLocationSource "identity_address"|"ip_address"|"payment_method"|"shipping_address"

---Default Billing settings for the customer account, used in Invoices and Subscriptions.
---@class stripe.V2CoreAccountConfigurationCustomerBilling
---@field default_payment_method? string The ID of a `PaymentMethod` attached to this Account's `customer` configuration, used as the default payment method for invoices and subscriptions.
---@field invoice? stripe.V2CoreAccountConfigurationCustomerBillingInvoice Default invoice settings for the customer account.

---Default invoice settings for the customer account.
---@class stripe.V2CoreAccountConfigurationCustomerBillingInvoice
---@field custom_fields stripe.V2CoreAccountConfigurationCustomerBillingInvoiceCustomFieldsList The list of up to 4 default custom fields to be displayed on invoices for this customer. When updating, pass an empty string to remove previously-defined fields.
---@field footer? string Default invoice footer.
---@field next_sequence? number Sequence number to use on the customer account's next invoice. Defaults to 1.
---@field prefix? string Prefix used to generate unique invoice numbers. Must be 3-12 uppercase letters or numbers.
---@field rendering? stripe.V2CoreAccountConfigurationCustomerBillingInvoiceRendering Default invoice PDF rendering options.

---@class stripe.V2CoreAccountConfigurationCustomerBillingInvoiceCustomFieldsItem
---@field name string The name of the custom field. This may be up to 40 characters.
---@field value string The value of the custom field. This may be up to 140 characters. When updating, pass an empty string to remove previously-defined values.

---The list of up to 4 default custom fields to be displayed on invoices for this customer. When updating, pass an empty string to remove previously-defined fields.
---@alias stripe.V2CoreAccountConfigurationCustomerBillingInvoiceCustomFieldsList stripe.V2CoreAccountConfigurationCustomerBillingInvoiceCustomFieldsItem[]

---Default invoice PDF rendering options.
---@class stripe.V2CoreAccountConfigurationCustomerBillingInvoiceRendering
---@field amount_tax_display? stripe.V2CoreAccountConfigurationCustomerBillingInvoiceRenderingAmountTaxDisplay Indicates whether displayed line item prices and amounts on invoice PDFs include inclusive tax amounts. Must be either `include_inclusive_tax` or `exclude_tax`.
