---Account Links let a platform create a temporary, single-use URL that an account can use to access a Stripe-hosted flow for collecting or updating required information.
---@class stripe.V2CoreAccountLink
---@field account string The ID of the connected account this Account Link applies to.
---@field created string The timestamp at which this Account Link was created.
---@field expires_at string The timestamp at which this Account Link will expire.
---@field livemode boolean Has the value `true` if the object exists in live mode or the value `false` if the object exists in test mode.
---@field object stripe.V2CoreAccountLinkObject String representing the object's type. Objects of the same type share the same value of the object field.
---@field url string The URL at which the account can access the Stripe-hosted flow.
---@field use_case stripe.V2CoreAccountLinkUseCase Describes the Stripe-hosted flow for this Account Link, including its type and flow-specific configuration.

---String representing the object's type. Objects of the same type share the same value of the object field.
---@alias stripe.V2CoreAccountLinkObject "v2.core.account_link"

---Describes the Stripe-hosted flow for this Account Link, including its type and flow-specific configuration.
---@class stripe.V2CoreAccountLinkUseCase
---@field account_onboarding? stripe.V2CoreAccountLinkUseCaseAccountOnboarding Hash containing configuration options for an Account Link object that onboards a new account.
---@field account_update? stripe.V2CoreAccountLinkUseCaseAccountUpdate Hash containing configuration options for an Account Link that updates an existing account.
---@field type stripe.V2CoreAccountLinkUseCaseType Open Enum. The type of Account Link the user is requesting.

---Hash containing configuration options for an Account Link object that onboards a new account.
---@class stripe.V2CoreAccountLinkUseCaseAccountOnboarding
---@field collection_options? stripe.V2CoreAccountLinkUseCaseAccountOnboardingCollectionOptions Specifies the requirements that Stripe collects from v2/core/accounts in the Onboarding flow.
---@field refresh_url string The URL the user will be redirected to if the AccountLink is expired, has been used, or is otherwise invalid. The URL you specify should attempt to generate a new AccountLink with the same parameters used to create the original AccountLink, then redirect the user to the new AccountLink’s URL so they can continue the flow. If a new AccountLink cannot be generated or the redirect fails you should display a useful error to the user. Please make sure to implement authentication before redirecting the user in case this URL is leaked to a third party.
---@field return_url? string The URL that the user will be redirected to upon completing the linked flow.

---Specifies the requirements that Stripe collects from v2/core/accounts in the Onboarding flow.
---@class stripe.V2CoreAccountLinkUseCaseAccountOnboardingCollectionOptions
---@field fields? stripe.V2CoreAccountLinkUseCaseAccountOnboardingCollectionOptionsFields Specifies whether the platform collects only currently_due requirements (`currently_due`) or both currently_due and eventually_due requirements (`eventually_due`). If you don’t specify collection_options, the default value is currently_due.
---@field future_requirements? stripe.V2CoreAccountLinkUseCaseAccountOnboardingCollectionOptionsFutureRequirements Specifies whether the platform collects future_requirements in addition to requirements in Connect Onboarding. The default value is `omit`.

---Specifies whether the platform collects only currently_due requirements (`currently_due`) or both currently_due and eventually_due requirements (`eventually_due`). If you don’t specify collection_options, the default value is currently_due.
---@alias stripe.V2CoreAccountLinkUseCaseAccountOnboardingCollectionOptionsFields "currently_due"|"eventually_due"

---Specifies whether the platform collects future_requirements in addition to requirements in Connect Onboarding. The default value is `omit`.
---@alias stripe.V2CoreAccountLinkUseCaseAccountOnboardingCollectionOptionsFutureRequirements "include"|"omit"

---Hash containing configuration options for an Account Link that updates an existing account.
---@class stripe.V2CoreAccountLinkUseCaseAccountUpdate
---@field collection_options? stripe.V2CoreAccountLinkUseCaseAccountUpdateCollectionOptions Specifies the requirements that Stripe collects from v2/core/accounts in the Onboarding flow.
---@field refresh_url string The URL the user will be redirected to if the Account Link is expired, has been used, or is otherwise invalid. The URL you specify should attempt to generate a new Account Link with the same parameters used to create the original Account Link, then redirect the user to the new Account Link URL so they can continue the flow. Make sure to authenticate the user before redirecting to the new Account Link, in case the URL leaks to a third party. If a new Account Link can't be generated, or if the redirect fails, you should display a useful error to the user.
---@field return_url? string The URL that the user will be redirected to upon completing the linked flow.

---Specifies the requirements that Stripe collects from v2/core/accounts in the Onboarding flow.
---@class stripe.V2CoreAccountLinkUseCaseAccountUpdateCollectionOptions
---@field fields? stripe.V2CoreAccountLinkUseCaseAccountUpdateCollectionOptionsFields Specifies whether the platform collects only currently_due requirements (`currently_due`) or both currently_due and eventually_due requirements (`eventually_due`). The default value is `currently_due`.
---@field future_requirements? stripe.V2CoreAccountLinkUseCaseAccountUpdateCollectionOptionsFutureRequirements Specifies whether the platform collects future_requirements in addition to requirements in Connect Onboarding. The default value is `omit`.

---Specifies whether the platform collects only currently_due requirements (`currently_due`) or both currently_due and eventually_due requirements (`eventually_due`). The default value is `currently_due`.
---@alias stripe.V2CoreAccountLinkUseCaseAccountUpdateCollectionOptionsFields "currently_due"|"eventually_due"

---Specifies whether the platform collects future_requirements in addition to requirements in Connect Onboarding. The default value is `omit`.
---@alias stripe.V2CoreAccountLinkUseCaseAccountUpdateCollectionOptionsFutureRequirements "include"|"omit"

---Open Enum. The type of Account Link the user is requesting.
---@alias stripe.V2CoreAccountLinkUseCaseType "account_onboarding"|"account_update"

