---A Transaction records how a money movement flow affects your FinancialAccount balance.
---A flow can create one or more Transactions.
---@class stripe.V2MoneyManagementTransaction
---@field amount stripe.V2MoneyManagementTransactionAmount The amount of the Transaction.
---@field balance_impact stripe.V2MoneyManagementTransactionBalanceImpact The change to the FinancialAccount's balance. This is the sum of the balance impacts of this Transaction's TransactionEntries with `effective_at` timestamps in the past.
---@field category stripe.V2MoneyManagementTransactionCategory Open Enum. A category used to classify the Transaction.
---@field counterparty? stripe.V2MoneyManagementTransactionCounterparty Details about the counterparty to this Transaction.
---@field created string Time at which the object was created. Represented as an RFC 3339 timestamp in UTC with millisecond precision, for example `2022-09-18T13:22:18.123Z`.
---@field description? string A description of the Transaction. When applicable, the description is copied from the flow object when the Transaction is created. You can update it using the Update Transaction endpoint.
---@field financial_account string The ID of the FinancialAccount affected by this Transaction.
---@field flow? stripe.V2MoneyManagementTransactionFlow Details about the flow object that created the Transaction, such as an InboundTransfer or OutboundPayment. `flow.type` identifies the kind of object. The corresponding field contains its ID, when available: for an InboundTransfer, `flow.inbound_transfer` contains the InboundTransfer's ID. Pass that ID to the `flow` parameter on List Transactions.
---@field id string Unique identifier for the object.
---@field livemode boolean Has the value `true` if the object exists in live mode or the value `false` if the object exists in test mode.
---@field metadata? stripe.V2MoneyManagementTransactionMetadataMap Set of key-value pairs that you can attach to an object. This can be useful for storing additional information about the object in a structured format.
---@field object stripe.V2MoneyManagementTransactionObject String representing the object's type. Objects of the same type share the same value of the object field.
---@field regulatory_receipt stripe.V2MoneyManagementTransactionRegulatoryReceipt Hosted transaction receipt that is provided when money movement is considered regulated under Stripe's money transmission licenses. If not applicable, `regulatory_receipt.status` will be `not_applicable` and no URL will be provided unless you opt in by calling `/refresh_regulatory_receipt`.
---@field status stripe.V2MoneyManagementTransactionStatus Closed Enum. The current status of the Transaction. A Transaction is `pending` if either `balance_impact.inbound_pending` or `balance_impact.outbound_pending` is non-zero. A Transaction is `posted` if only `balance_impact.available` is non-zero. A Transaction is `void` if there is no balance impact. `posted` and `void` are terminal states, and no additional TransactionEntries will be added to the Transaction.
---@field status_transitions stripe.V2MoneyManagementTransactionStatusTransitions Timestamps for when the Transaction transitioned to each status.

