---Create an account
---
---<p>With <a href="/docs/connect">Connect</a>, you can create Stripe accounts for your users.
---To do this, you’ll first need to <a href="https://dashboard.stripe.com/account/applications/settings">register your platform</a>.</p>
---
---<p>If you’ve already collected information for your connected accounts, you <a href="/connect/marketplace/tasks/create#prefill-account-information">can prefill that information</a> when
---creating the account. Connect Onboarding won’t ask for the prefilled information during account onboarding.
---You can prefill any information on the account.</p>
---
---`POST /v1/accounts`
---@param input? stripe.CreateAccountRequest
---@return stripe.Account? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:create_account(input) end

---Create an external account
---
---<p>Create an external account for a given account.</p>
---
---`POST /v1/accounts/{account}/external_accounts`
---@param input stripe.CreateAccountExternalAccountRequest
---@return stripe.ExternalAccount? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:create_account_external_account(input) end

---Create an account link
---
---<p>Creates an AccountLink object that includes a single-use Stripe URL that the platform can redirect their user to in order to take them through the Connect Onboarding flow.</p>
---
---`POST /v1/account_links`
---@param input stripe.CreateAccountLinkRequest
---@return stripe.AccountLink? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:create_account_link(input) end

---Create a login link
---
---<p>Creates a login link for a connected account to access the Express Dashboard.</p>
---
---<p><strong>You can only create login links for accounts that use the <a href="/connect/express-dashboard">Express Dashboard</a> and are connected to your platform</strong>.</p>
---
---`POST /v1/accounts/{account}/login_links`
---@param input stripe.CreateAccountLoginLinkRequest
---@return stripe.LoginLink? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:create_account_login_link(input) end

---Create a person
---
---<p>Creates a new person.</p>
---
---`POST /v1/accounts/{account}/persons`
---@param input stripe.CreateAccountPersonRequest
---@return stripe.Person? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:create_account_person(input) end

---Reject an account
---
---<p>With <a href="/connect">Connect</a>, you can reject accounts that you have flagged as suspicious.</p>
---
---<p>Only accounts where your platform is liable for negative account balances, which includes Custom and Express accounts, can be rejected.</p>
---
---`POST /v1/accounts/{account}/reject`
---@param input stripe.CreateAccountRejectRequest
---@return stripe.Account? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:create_account_reject(input) end

---Create an Account Session
---
---<p>Creates an AccountSession object that includes a single-use token that the platform can use on their front-end to grant client-side API access.</p>
---
---`POST /v1/account_sessions`
---@param input stripe.CreateAccountSessionRequest
---@return stripe.AccountSession? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:create_account_session(input) end

---Unreject an account
---
---<p>With Connect, you can unreject accounts that you have previously rejected.</p>
---
---<p>Only accounts that were rejected by your platform can be unrejected. This API cannot be used to unreject accounts that were rejected by Stripe.</p>
---
---<p>Unreject will only enable charges and/or payouts if there are no other restrictions other than those placed by a previous rejection. If you have separately paused charges and/or payouts outside of rejection, those pauses will remain in place after unrejection.</p>
---
---`POST /v1/accounts/{account}/unreject`
---@param input stripe.CreateAccountUnrejectRequest
---@return stripe.Account? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:create_account_unreject(input) end

---<p>Create an apple pay domain.</p>
---
---`POST /v1/apple_pay/domains`
---@param input stripe.CreateApplePayDomainRequest
---@return stripe.ApplePayDomain? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:create_apple_pay_domain(input) end

---Create an application fee refund
---
---<p>Refunds an application fee that has previously been collected but not yet refunded.
---Funds will be refunded to the Stripe account from which the fee was originally collected.</p>
---
---<p>You can optionally refund only part of an application fee.
---You can do so multiple times, until the entire fee has been refunded.</p>
---
---<p>Once entirely refunded, an application fee can’t be refunded again.
---This method will raise an error when called on an already-refunded application fee,
---or when trying to refund more money than is left on an application fee.</p>
---
---`POST /v1/application_fees/{id}/refunds`
---@param input stripe.CreateApplicationFeeRefundRequest
---@return stripe.FeeRefund? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:create_application_fee_refund(input) end

---Create an app install
---
---<p>Creates an app install. An account installs its own private app with its own key; public and testing installs are made from the Dashboard. An app developer acting on a connected account through <code>Stripe-Account</code> installs or reinstalls its app there, and an embedding platform can do the same once the app’s developer approves its request to embed the app. For a private app, creating an install installs the newest completed upload; when that version is already installed with nothing pending, the existing install is returned.</p>
---
---`POST /v1/apps/installs`
---@param input stripe.CreateAppsInstallRequest
---@return stripe.AppsInstall? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:create_apps_install(input) end

---Uninstall an app install
---
---<p>Uninstalls an app from the account that installed it.</p>
---
---`POST /v1/apps/installs/{id}/uninstall`
---@param input stripe.CreateAppsInstallUninstallRequest
---@return stripe.AppsInstall? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:create_apps_install_uninstall(input) end

---Set a Secret
---
---<p>Create or replace a secret in the secret store.</p>
---
---`POST /v1/apps/secrets`
---@param input stripe.CreateAppsSecretRequest
---@return stripe.AppsSecret? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:create_apps_secret(input) end

---Delete a Secret
---
---<p>Deletes a secret from the secret store by name and scope.</p>
---
---`POST /v1/apps/secrets/delete`
---@param input stripe.CreateAppsSecretsDeleteRequest
---@return stripe.AppsSecret? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:create_apps_secrets_delete(input) end

---Update balance settings
---
---<p>Updates balance settings for a given connected account.
--- Related guide: <a href="/connect/authentication">Making API calls for connected accounts</a></p>
---
---`POST /v1/balance_settings`
---@param input? stripe.CreateBalanceSettingsRequest
---@return stripe.BalanceSettings? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:create_balance_settings(input) end

---Create a billing alert
---
---<p>Creates a billing alert</p>
